[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m On a particular map, $3$ inches on the map equates to $10$ miles in real life. If you know that the real life distance between two buildings on the map is $53.25$ miles, what would the distance between the buildings be (in inches) on the map, expressed as a fraction?
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the distance between the buildings on the map, we can use the scale provided. The scale tells us that 3 inches on the map corresponds to 10 miles in real life. We need to find out how many inches correspond to 53.25 miles.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m First, we set up a proportion to find the number of inches that correspond to 53.25 miles:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \frac{3 \text{ inches}}{10 \text{ miles}} = \frac{x \text{ inches}}{53.25 \text{ miles}}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Solving for \( x \):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m x = \frac{3 \text{ inches} \times 53.25 \text{ miles}}{10 \text{ miles}}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m x = \frac{159.75 \text{ inches}}{10 \text{ miles}}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m x = 15.975 \text{ inches}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, the distance between the buildings on the map is \( 15.975 \) inches.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To express this as a fraction, we can write:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 15.975 = \frac{159.75}{1}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Thus, the distance between the buildings on the map, expressed as a fraction, is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \boxed{\frac{159.75}{1}}
