[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the greatest common factor (GCF) of all two-digit palindromes, let's first identify the two-digit palindromes:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. Two-digit numbers are composed of a tens digit and ones digit: \(10 \times \_ \times \_ \) and \(9 \times \_ \times \_ \) respectively.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Calculations for all two-digit palindromes: 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m   - \(10 \times 8 \times 8 = 640\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m   - \(9 \times 9 \times 9 = 729\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now we'll list these values from smallest to largest:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \(640\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \(729\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The common factors we have found so far are 1 (as \(729\)) and 3 (as \(640\)). 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To consider the largest possible factors, let’s see if any factors exist. Given that both numbers are even, we might require even numbers to benefit the calculation.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We will consider \(3 x 3 \), \(5 x \times 5\) since they are factors that multiply evenly each time:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3) \(640\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 5) \(640 \div 5 = 128\) (large enough)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 6) \(640 \div 3 = 213\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 7) \(213 \div 3 = 71\) (also easy)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Without listing:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Thus, the GCF is 3. But considering large even numbers provides additional factors to ensure all pairs of palindromes are prime numbers (only includes 3 as factors):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \(\Rightarrow GCF(640, 729) = 3\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Putting this all together for everything in careful consecuence:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ```latex
