[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To determine the given matrices are inverses (i.e., \(A, B, A^{-1}, B^{-1}\) are the same matrix), we will start by calculating the inverse of each matrix and then checking if they are equal.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We will perform matrix multiplications and check if they yield the same result for all elements. First, let's compute \(A \cdot A^{-1}\) for the first matrix and check the result, and proceed similarly for the second matrix.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m A = \begin{pmatrix} a & 1 & b \\ 2 & 2 & 3 \\ c & 5 & d \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m A^{-1} = \begin{pmatrix} a^{-1} & -\frac{a^{-1} \cdot 1 + 1 - bc}{0} \\ -\frac{2 - 1 \cdot c}{a^{-1}} & -\frac{2 - 2 c}{0} \\ -\frac{3 - 5 d}{a^{-1}} & -\frac{3 - 5 d}{0} \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} a^{-1} & b^{-1} & c^{-1} \\ \infty & 2^{-1} & -2^{-1} \\ -2^{-1} & -2^{-1} & d^{-1} \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Matrix \(A^{-1}\) should be invertible if its determinant is non-zero. Computations:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ \det(A) = \det\left(\begin{pmatrix} a & 1 & b \\ 2 & 2 & 3 \\ c & 5 & d \end{pmatrix}\right) = \det\begin{pmatrix} a & 1 & 0 \\ 2 & 2 & 0 \\ c & 5 & d \end{pmatrix} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ = a \cdot (2 \cdot d - 5 \cdot c) - 1 \cdot (2 \cdot d - 5 \cdot c) + 0 \cdot (2 \cdot 2 - c \cdot 5) = a \cdot 2d - 5 \cdot 2c - dc + 2c + 0 = 2ad - 10c - dc + 2c = ad - 8c \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m For \(A\) and \(A^{-1}\) to be inverses, \(a \cdot 2d - 10c - dc + 2c = ad - 8c\), which simplifies to \(0 = 0\), confirms \(A\) can be inverted.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Next, for \(A^{-1}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ (A^{-1})A = \begin{pmatrix} a^{-1} & b^{-1} & c^{-1} \\ \infty & 2^{-1} & -2^{-1} \\ -2^{-1} & -2^{-1} & d^{-1} \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} a & 1 & b \\ 2 & 2 & 3 \\ c & 5 & d \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} a^{2^{-1}} + 2^{-1}c & a^{1} + 2^{-1}b & b^{1} + 2^{-1}3 \\ 2^{-1}a^{2^{-1}} + c^{2^{-1}} & 2^{-1}a^{1} + 2^{-1}b^{1} & 2^{-1}b^{1} + 2^{-1}3 \\ c^{2^{-1}} - 2^{-2} \cdot 2^{-1}c - 2^{-2} \cdot 2^{-1}d & c^{1} + 2^{-1}d + 2^{-1}2^{-2} & c^{1} + 2^{-1}d + 2^{-1}2^{-2} \end{pmatrix} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m For non-zero determinant (\(\det(A^{-1}) = ad - 8c \neq 0\)),
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ a^{2^{-1}} + 2^{-1}c = a + b + c^2 + 2b + d^2 - 2c \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Hence, substituting the terms for each equation into one diagonal element \(a^{2^{-1}} + 2^{-1}c\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ a^{2^{-1}} + 2^{-1}c = a + b + c^2 + 2b + d^2 - 2c \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ a + b + c^2 + 2b + d^2 - 2c = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Simplifying, \(a + b + c^2 + 2b + d^2 - 2c = 2(b + c + d)\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ 2(a + b + c^2 + d^2 - 3c - 2b) = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Hence:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ a + b + c^2 + d^2 - 3c - 2b = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, combining all equations term by term:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ a + b + c + m + n = \boxed{16} \]<|endoftext|>
