[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let $a = \log_2 (27+ \log_2 (27+ \log_2 (27+ \cdots)))$ Suppose $z$ is a positive constant such that $a=z$, then we have \begin{aligned} x &= 27 + \log_2 (27+ \log_2 (27+ \log_2 (27+ \cdots)))\\ &= 27 + \log_2 x, \end{aligned} that means the above equation has the solution $x=27^\log_2 z$, that is of the form $x = y^z$ where $\color{#00f}{y = 27^\log_2 z}$ In this case, we have $y = z$.Thus the expression for $a$ is $a=z=z^\log_2 z=z^{1+\log_2 z} =$ Also since $z>0$ and $y=z$,we have $z^{\log_2 z}=z^\log_2 z$<|endoftext|>
