[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We have the following equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \displaystyle \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m x &= y + 5\\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m y &= z + 10\\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m z &= w + 20\\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \text{and }\qquad w &= 80
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Starting with the fifth equation, we can substitute \(w = 80\) into the third equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 80 = w + 20 \implies 80 = 80 + 20 \implies 80 = 100 + 80
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, add those numbers together:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 80 + 80 + 100 &= x + 600\\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 260 & &= x + 600
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
