[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. First, combine the terms with a single fraction over the same denominator by adding them together:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\frac{2}{x} + \frac{1}{x} - \frac{3}{5}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Simplify the addition and subtraction of fractions:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\frac{3}{x} - \frac{3}{5}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. Simplify the left side by finding a common denominator (which in this case is 5):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\frac{15}{5x} - \frac{3x}{5x}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4. Simplify further on the lower term:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\frac{15 - 3x}{5x}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 5. Simplify the common denominator on the numerator:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\frac{15 - 3x}{5x} = \frac{15}{5x} - \frac{3x}{5x}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 6. Cancel out the common denominator $5x$:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\frac{15 - 3x}{5x} = \frac{15}{5x} - \frac{3x}{5x} = \frac{15 - 3x}{5x}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, we have the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\frac{15 - 3x}{5} = \frac{1}{5}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 7. Since both sides have a common denominator, cross multiply to eliminate the fractions:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$15 - 3x = 1$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 8. Solve for $x$ by isolating it on one side:
