[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the sum of the numbers in Row 8 of Pascal's Triangle, we need to sum all the elements in the third row (up to and including Row 8). 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The remaining elements in Row 8 can be found by examining the values:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - The last element in Row 3 is $3$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - The second-to-last element in Row 4 is $6$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - The last element in Row 5 is $10$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The sum of these elements gives us the third row's values:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - Summed: $3 + 6 + 10 = 19$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, the sum of the numbers in Row 8 of Pascal's Triangle is $\boxed{19}$.
