[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The bagel shop has enough benches to sit $204_6$ people. If $2$ people are supposed to sit on one bench, how many benches does the shop have?
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We are given that the total number of seats in the bagel shop is $204.6\text{ }=\text{ }203$ benches and that $2$ people are supposed to sit on one bench. 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find how many benches there are in total, we need to divide the total number of seats by the number of people that can sit on each bench.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $204.6\text{ }=\text{ }203$ benches.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Since the number of benches can only be a whole number, we need to round up to the nearest whole number because we cannot have a fraction of a bench.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $\lceil{203\text{ }=\text{ }203.0}\\ \rceil = 204$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So the shop has $204$ benches.<|endoftext|>
