[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  Jessica starts by reasoning that she can make 30 pies and use 30 cups of flour during bake time. 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Jessica would originally make another 15 larger pies with the same amount of flour. Calculating the amount of flour consumed will require making 30 powder pie crust pieces and then using 15 times the amount that she used to bake 20 smaller pies.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Jessica calculates it to be: 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{array}{r}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 30\times30=900 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 15\times900=1350
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Jessica tells her boss that she can make 3 larger pies in the same amount of flour, and she needs to multiply this by the 15 larger pies to get a total provision of 153 pies with the same amount of flour. Mathematically, this is represented as:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{array}{rcl}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 900\times15&=&1350\\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1350\times15&=&153
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The calculation of 1350 cups of flour yields, "*placeholder*", as it doesn't affect the amount of pie crust pieces nor the remaining flour used to bake other items after making 20 larger pies, which are accounted for in the *placeholder*.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Combining all the items yields Jessica's answer being:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \boxed{153} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m cupshfill 3 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \meaning {
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m     The amount of flour generated in 30 larger pie crusts with the same amount of flour as 20 smaller pies is reported as 153 cups of flour. This leaves no processed ingredients not utilized compared to the additional 153 cups of flour, thereby explaining the observation with 32 larger pie crusts.}
