[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the minimum perimeter among all 8-sided polygons in the complex plane whose vertices are the zeros of the polynomial $P(z)$, we need to find the critical points of the polynomial $P(z)$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Given the polynomial:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m P(z) = z^8 + (4\sqrt{3} + 6)z^4 - (4\sqrt{3} + 7)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We can differentiate $P(z)$ with respect to $z$ and set it to zero to find the critical points:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We have $P(z) = z^8 + (4\sqrt{3} + 6)z^4 - (4\sqrt{3} + 7)$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m P'(z) = 8z^7 + 4(4\sqrt{3} + 6)z^3 - 4\sqrt{3}.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Setting $P'(z) = 0$:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 8z^7 + 4(4\sqrt{3} + 6)z^3 - 4\sqrt{3} = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Solving for z:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m (8z^7 + 4(4\sqrt{3} + 6)z^3 - 4\sqrt{3}) = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 8z^7 + 4(4\sqrt{3} + 6)z^3 - 4\sqrt{3} = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4(4\sqrt{3} + 6)z^3 - 4\sqrt{3} = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1 + 2\sqrt{3} = \frac{4\sqrt{3} - 4}{4z^3}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \frac{(4\sqrt{3} + 6)}{4} = \frac{4\sqrt{3} - 4}{4z^3}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \frac{(4\sqrt{3} + 6)}{4}z^3 = 4\sqrt{3} - 4
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m z^3 = \frac{4\sqrt{3}(4\sqrt{3} + 6)}{(4\sqrt{3} - 4)} = \frac{48 + 24}{(4\sqrt{3} - 4)} = \frac{72}{20\sqrt{3} - 16} = \frac{72}{-8\sqrt{3} + 8} = \frac{36}{-4\sqrt{3} + 4} = \frac{36\sqrt{3}}{4} = 9\sqrt{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Since the solutions are of the form $z =(-1\pm 5i)^{1/3}$, we need to compute the absolute values of these roots.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let's calculate:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $|\cop ((-1+5i)_{1/3})| = |{-1+5i}| = \sqrt{(-1)^2 + (5)^2} = \sqrt{1 + 25} = \sqrt{26} \approx 5.1\sqrt{2}$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $|\cop ((-1-5i)_{1/3})| = |{-1-5i}| = \sqrt{(-1)^2 + (-5)^2} = \sqrt{1 + 25} = \sqrt{26} \approx 5.1\sqrt{2}$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The minimum perimeter will occur when two of the roots are the same and the third root has the minimum distance. Since we have only two roots, we need to choose one of them and consider the third root.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Without loss of generality, let's use the root $(-1 + 5i)_{1/3}$ that yields the smaller absolute value. The perimeter will be:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Perimeter = $2 \times 9\sqrt{3}$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Perimeter = $18\sqrt{3}$
