[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the least, positive four-digit multiple of 7, we start by identifying the smallest four-digit number, which is 1000.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Next, we divide 1000 by 7 to find the quotient and remainder:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1000 ÷ 7 = 142 with a remainder 6.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We know that any multiple of 7 will have a remainder of 6 when divided by 7, so we need to find a multiple of 7 right after 142.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Division by 7 yields a quotient of 142 and a remainder of 6.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We can then multiply 142 by 7 to find the next multiple of 7:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 142 * 7 = 994
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, the least, positive four-digit multiple of 7 is 994.
