[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the number of integers in the solution of the inequality \( |x + 4| < 9 \), we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. **Understand the Absolute Value Inequality:**
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    The inequality \( |x + 4| < 9 \) can be interpreted graphically or mathematically. It states that the distance between \( x \) and \(-4\) is less than 9. This can be broken down as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    -13 < x + 4 < 12
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    This inequality separates two parts: \(-13 < x + 4\) and \(x + 4 < 12\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. **Solve Each Part Separately:**
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - For the first part of the inequality, \(-13 < x + 4\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      Subtract 4 from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      -13 - 4 < x
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      Simplify:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      -17 < x \quad \text{(or} \quad x > -17\text{)}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - For the second part of the inequality, \(x + 4 < 12\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      Subtract 4 from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      x < 12 - 4
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      Simplify:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      x < 8
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    Combine the two parts:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    -17 < x \quad \text{and} \quad x < 8
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    This gives us the interval:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    -17 < x < 8
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. **Identify the Integers in the Interval:**
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
