[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the product of the digits in the base 8 representation of 6543 in base 10, we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. Convert the base 10 number to base 8.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Multiply the base 8 representation to get the product.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Base 10 number: 6543
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 1: Convert the base 10 number to base 8:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To convert a number from base 10 to base 8, we repeatedly divide the number by 8 and keep track of the remainders.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 6543 ÷ 8 = 817 remainder 7
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 817 ÷ 8 = 102 remainder 5
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 102 ÷ 8 = 12 remainder 6
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 12 ÷ 8 = 1 remainder 4
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1 ÷ 8 = 0 remainder 1
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, the base 8 representation of 6543 is 14657.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 2: Multiply the base 8 representation to get the product:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 14657 × 7 = 102509
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, the product of the digits in the base 8 representation of 6543 in base 10 is 102509.
