[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Simplify $(2x - 5)(x + 7) - (x + 5)(2x - 1)$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 1: Evaluate $(2x - 5)(x + 7) - (x + 5)(2x - 1)$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We start with the parenthesized parts:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - $(2x - 5)$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - $(x + 7)$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - $(x + 5)$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - $(2x - 1)$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 2: Apply the distributive property (FOIL) to each set of parentheses.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - $(2x - 5)(x + 7) = 2x(x + 7) - 5(x + 7) = 2x^2 + 14x - 5x - 35 = 2x^2 + 9x - 35$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - $(x + 5)(2x - 1) = x(2x) + 5(2x) - x(1) - 5(1) = 2x^2 + 10x - x - 5 = 2x^2 + 9x - 5$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 3: Combine the simplified parts.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $2x^2 + 9x - 35 - (2x^2 + 9x - 5) = 2x^2 + 9x - 35 - 2x^2 - 9x + 5$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 4: Combine like terms.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $2x^2 + 2x^2 + 9x - 9x - 35 + 5 = 4x^2 + 8 - 30 = 4x^2 - 22$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 5: Write the final result in the boxed format.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m boxed{4x^2 - 22}
