[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To convert $813_9$ to base 3, we need to convert the number into base 10 and then convert the result into base 3.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. Converting $813_9$ to base 10:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$813_9 = 8 \times 9^2 + 1 \times 9^1 + 3 \times 9^0$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$813_9 = 8 \times 81 + 1 \times 9 + 3$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$813_9 = 648 + 9 + 3$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$813_9 = 651$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, $813_9$ in base 10 is 651.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Converting 651 to base 3:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$651_{10}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Divide by 3:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$651 ÷ 3 = 217$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$217 ÷ 3 = 72$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$72 ÷ 3 = 24$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$24 ÷ 3 = 8$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$8 ÷ 3 = 2$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$2 ÷ 3 = 0$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, we're left with 28, which is a non-zero digit.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, the base 3 representation of 651 is 2831.
