[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find $f(g(-3))$ , we will follow the way we would solve an equation with exponents and then solve for $f(x)$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m For the right-hand side of the equation, first, we will substitute in $-3$ into the expression of $g(x)$ to get $g(-3) = 3(-3) + 4$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m After evaluating $g(-3)$, we should proceed and plug this value into the original function $f(x)$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $\color{blue}{\boxed{}=[color{blue}{x^2}]}$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $\color{red}{}\forall  \color{red} x \in \left(-∞,-3 \right\cup \left(+3,+∞\right)}$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $\color{blue}[color{red}{x^2}-2x+1]$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $\color{blue}=[color{blue}{(x-1)^2}]$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $\color{blue}=-3$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $\color{blue}{\frac{f(g(-3))}{g(-3)}}=\frac{-3^2}{-3}$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $\color{blue}=-3$
