[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To solve for \(\angle DAC\) and \(\angle ADE\), we will use geometric properties, particularly involving angles formed by a transversal crossing parallel lines. Let's start by analyzing the given information and steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. Given \(\angle BAC = 20^\circ\) and \(\angle EDF = 30^\circ\), we know they form straight angles because \(DE\) is a transversal with lines \(AD\) and \(DF\). Thus, \(\angle ADE\) and \(\angle EDF\) together form straight angles:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m     \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m     \angle ADE + \angle EDF = 180^\circ.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m     \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    So,
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m     \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m     \angle DAC = 180^\circ - \angle ADE \quad \text{(because \(AB = AC\), making \(\triangle ABC\) is isosceles, thus \(\angle ACB = 20^\circ\) and \(\angle BAC = 20^\circ\))}.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m     \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Now let’s consider the angles \(\angle BAC\), \(\angle EDF\), and \(\angle DAC\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - We have \(\angle EDF \) 30 degrees, and 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      \angle BAC = 20^\circ \implies \angle ABC = 20^\circ.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m     \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - \(\angle DAC\), being part of the arc \(\widehat{BC}\) cut by \(AD\) with an angle of \(180-\angle BAC = 180^\circ - 20^\circ = 160^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the steps to calculate \(\angle DAC\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \(\angle BAC = 20^\circ\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \(\angle ACB = 20^\circ\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \(\angle EDF = 30^\circ\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Considering \(\angle DAC = 160^\circ\) (since it's part of equally drawn shifts) results in more complicated approach. But also, looping looks optimal it follows a reasonable approach with remaining ways to observances and approximation mistakes as mentioned in diversified empty code fit.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  
