[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Four times $x$ is congruent to eight modulo twenty. If four times $x$ is intense, eight modulo twenty, then $3x$ is congruent to eighteen modulo twenty. The remainder when $(3x)^2=81$ is squared, recalling that the remainder is rearranged after the modular exponentiation. Therefore, the remainder when $81$ is cubed is $3$.
