[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m First case: the product of two positive whole numbers can be directly calculated. This requires that one of the numbers is 1. In this case, as 1×1=1, we have 1 being a divisor of 2005.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We know 2005 cannot be evenly divided by 1, hence it can not be divided by 1. Therefore, for any other numbers, we can cancel out both factors in the division. Through this reasoning and calculation, we realize that the numbers are 101 and 201.
