[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m In the diagram, $AB = 25 \mbox{ cm},$ $AC = 20 \mbox{ cm},$ and $\angle A = 90^\circ.$ What is the area of triangle $ABC?$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m [asy]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m draw((0,0)--(25,0)--(0,20)--cycle,black+linewidth(1));
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m draw((0,0)--(1,0)--(1,1)--(0,1)--cycle,black+linewidth(1));
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m label("$A$",(0,0),SW);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m label("$B$",(25,0),SE);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m label("$C$",(0,20),NW);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m [/asy]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the area of triangle \(ABC\), we can use the formula for the area of a right triangle. The formula is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \times \text{base} \times \text{height} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m In this particular problem, we are given the lengths of two sides and an angle of 90 degrees. In a right-angled triangle, the two legs are the base and height. So we will use this information effectively.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m In triangle \(ABC\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - The base \(AB\) is 25 cm.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - The height \(AC\) is 20 cm.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - The angle between side \(AB\) and side \(AC\) is 90 degrees.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, we multiply the lengths of the base and the height to get the area in square centimeters.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let's perform the calculation in Python.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ```python
