[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To solve for $x,$ we'll first isolate the exponential term. To do this, we'll divide both sides by 2:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\dfrac{2(3^x) = 162}{2}=\\[10pt]{3^x= 81}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Our goal will now be to figure out what the value of $x$ is.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m In order to do this, we'll want to bring all words on one side of the equation and numbers on the other. We can do this by raising both the number and the exponential term to the power of the same value, which will introduce imaginary numbers as an answer.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$3^x = 81 \\[50pt] {3^2}^x = {3^4}^3 {3^3}^x = {3^5}^2 \\[50pt] {3}^x = {3}^{20}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We'll notice that the left side has the same power as the right side, so we can set the exponents equal to one another:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $${3}^x = {3}^{20} \\[50pt] x = 20$$
