[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Find $\cot (-60^\circ).$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To determine the value of $\cot(-60^\circ)$, we can use the definition of cotangent function: 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \cot(x) & = \frac{1}{\tan(x)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m & = \frac{\cos(x)}{\sin(x)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m & = \frac{1}{p/q} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m where $p$ and $q$ are the factors to multiply the square root in the denominator.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let's first simplify the absolute value to remove the negative sign:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \cot(-60^\circ) &= \frac{1}{\tan(-60^\circ)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= \frac{1}{(-\tan(60^\circ))} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= \frac{1}{-\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= \boxed{ -\frac{2}{\sqrt{3}} }
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}<|endoftext|>
