[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 5. Each number \( n \) in this range, which is within 20, results in \( \sqrt{n} \) being greater than or equal to 8. Thus, there are ten such numbers in the range 20 to 99 inclusive - hence the total.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 6.  The probability that a randomly selected two-digit number \( n \) results in \( \sqrt{n} \geq 8 \) can be found as a fraction of the total numbers in the range.
