[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To compute $(3^2)(2^4)(37)(5^3)$, we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 1: Compute $(3^2)$, which is equivalent to $(3 \times 3)$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $(3^2) = 3 \times 3 = 9$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 2: Compute $(2^4)$, which is equivalent to $(2 \times 2 \times 2 \times 2)$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $(2^4) = 2 \times 2 \times 2 \times 2 = 16$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 3: Compute $37$, which is already a single number.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 4: Compute $(5^3)$, which is equivalent to $(5 \times 5 \times 5)$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $(5^3) = 5 \times 5 \times 5 = 125$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now we multiply all the computed values together:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $9 \times 16 \times 37 \times 125$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 5: Calculate the product of 9, 16, 37, and 125.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $9 \times 16 = 144$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $144 \times 37 = 5472$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $5472 \times 125 = 688000$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, the answer is $\boxed{688000}$.<|endoftext|>
