[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m First, we want to factorize $ \dfrac{4x}{(x - 5)(x - 3)^2}= \dfrac{A}{x - 5} + \dfrac{B}{x - 3} + \dfrac{C}{(x - 3)^2}$, so we need to do the following:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \dfrac{4x}{(x - 5)(x - 3)^2} &= \dfrac{4(x - 3)(x + 1)}{(x - 5)(x - 3)(x + 2)(x - 3)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= \dfrac{A}{x - 5} + \dfrac{B (x + 2)}{(x - 3)(x + 1)} + \dfrac{C (x - 3)}{(x - 5)(x - 3)(x + 1)}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m If we will come across any factors in the denominator with the same $(x - 3),$ we will set the index equal to the pair's index; that way, we can always factor out the factor in the denominator. This will give us:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \dfrac{4(x - 3)(x + 1)}{(x - 5)(x - 3)(x + 2)(x - 3)} &= \dfrac{4(x - 3)}{(x - 5)(x - 3)(x + 2)} + \dfrac{B (x + 2)}{(x - 3)(x + 1)} + \dfrac{C (x - 3)}{(x - 5)(x - 3)(x + 1)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= \dfrac{A + B (x + 2)}{x - 5} + \dfrac{C (x - 3)}{x - 3}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Lastly, if we look at the coefficients in the top equation and the left-hand-sides of the equation, we can see that $ \dfrac{A}{x - 5} + \dfrac{C(x - 3)}{x - 3} = \dfrac{A + C} {x - 5} $
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Hence, for this equation, we have that:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \boxed{(A + C , -4, \boxed{-1})}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  thankful for it<|endoftext|>
