[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To add 10_7 (base 7) and 163_7 (base 7) and express the result in base 7, follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 1: Change the numbers to base 10.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To do this, recall that in base 10, the values of digits increase from right to left. Therefore, 10_7 (base 7) is \(1 \times 7^1 + 0 \times 7^0 = 7\), and 163_7 (base 7) is \(1 \times 7^2 + 6 \times 7^1 + 3 \times 7^0 = 49 + 42 + 3 = 94\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 2: Sum the base 10 equivalents.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, add the base 10 numbers: \(7 + 94 = 101\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 3: Convert the sum to base 7.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To do this, repeatedly divide the sum by 7 and keep track of the remainders. The base 7 representation is the sequence of remainders read from bottom to top.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
