[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. For February 5, 1916, which is in the 22nd century, convert it to base 10:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ \text{date}_{1916} = 22 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. For February 5, 2000, convert it to base 10:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ \text{date}_{2000} = 25 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. Add these values together:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ \text{date}_{1916} + \text{date}_{2000} = 22 + 25 = 47\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4. Now convert 47 to base 7 (since we are working within the 22nd century):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - Theًا · 7 Fits (なんだしての) gets the 1st digit, i.e., 4
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - The remainder stays at 7
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    So, 47_10 is 125_7
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, the answer is 125_7.
