[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Sure, let's factor the expression $7x^2 - 63$ step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. Identify the common binomial factor: We see that both terms in the expression have $7x$ as a common factor. So, we write $7x^2$ as a common factor.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    7x^2 &= 7x \times x \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    -63 &= 7 \times -9 \times x^2
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Factor out the common factor, which is $7x$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    7x^2 - 63 &= 7x(x) - 7x(-9) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    &= 7x(x + 9)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, the factored expression is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ \boxed{7x(x + 9)} \]<|endoftext|>
