[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find $f^{-1}(58)$, we need to find the value of $x$ such that $f(x)=58$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, we have $f(x)=58$, which means that $2x^3+4=58$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Subtracting 4 from both sides, we get $2x^3=54$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
