[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Simplify the product \[\frac{8}{4}\cdot\frac{12}{8}\cdot\frac{16}{12} \dotsm \frac{4n+4}{4n} \dotsm \frac{2008}{2004}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The product is $8 / (4)(8)(16) \dotsm (2n+4)(2n)$. We now note that all odd terms cancel and that for every two consecutive consecutive numbers, there is a term in the numerator and denominator that cancels out. So you are left with $8 / (4n+4)$ only. This needs to be simplified to $2 / n$.
