[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We're looking for a way to simplify \sqrt[3]{30p} \cdot \sqrt[3]{5p} \cdot \sqrt[3]{6p}.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To do this, we can apply the property of radicals that says:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{equation*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m a^n \cdot a^m = a^{n+m}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{equation*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Applying this, we have
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \sqrt[3]{30p} \cdot \sqrt[3]{5p} & = \sqrt[3]{30p \cdot 5p} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m & = \sqrt[3]{150p^2}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m and
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \sqrt[3]{150p^2} \cdot \sqrt[3]{6p} & = \sqrt[3]{150p^2 \cdot 6p} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m & = \sqrt[3]{900p^3}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m and finally,
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \sqrt[3]{900p^3} = \sqrt[3]{90 \cdot 3 \cdot p^2}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m and we're left with
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{equation*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \boxed{\sqrt[3]{30p} \sqrt[3]{5p} \sqrt[3]{6p} = \sqrt[3]{90p^3} = \sqrt[3]{30p \cdot 5p \cdot 6p} = \sqrt[3]{30p \cdot (5 \cdot p \cdot 6p)} = \sqrt[3]{30p \cdot 30p^2} = \sqrt[3]{30^2p^3}}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{equation*}<|endoftext|>
