[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Write the ratios in simplest form.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\begin{array}{l} \dfrac{ 3 }{ 5 } : \dfrac{ 9 }{ 10 } \qquad \dfrac{ 4 }{ 9 } : \dfrac{ 8 }{ 97 } \\ \dfrac{ 11 }{ 20 } : \dfrac{ 20 }{ 37 } \qquad \dfrac{ 5 }{ 6 } : \dfrac{ 10 }{ 63 } \end{array}$$ Let's simplify each ratio step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ### Ratio 1: \(\dfrac{ 3 }{ 5 } : \dfrac{ 9 }{ 10 }\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. Find the Least Common Denominator (LCD) of 5 and 10.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \text{LCD} = 10
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Convert \(\dfrac{ 3 }{ 5 }\) to an equivalent fraction with the LCD as the denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \dfrac{ 3 }{ 5 } = \dfrac{ 3 \times 2 }{ 5 \times 2 } = \dfrac{ 6 }{ 10 }
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. Now we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \dfrac{ 6 }{ 10 } : \dfrac{ 9 }{ 10 }
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4. Simplify by dividing the numerators and denominators by their greatest common divisor (GCD):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - GCD of 6 and 9 is 3, and we divide by 3 in both fractions:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      \dfrac{ 6 \div 3 }{ 10 \div 3 } = \dfrac{ 2 }{ \frac{ 10 }{ 3 } }
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 5. This becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \dfrac{ 2 }{ \frac{ 10 }{ 3 } } = 2 \times \dfrac{ 3 }{ 10 } = \dfrac{ 6 }{ 10 }
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 6. Simplify further:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - \(\dfrac{ 6 }{ 10 } = \dfrac{ 6 \div 2 }{ 10 \div 2 } = \dfrac{ 3 }{ 5 }
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ### Ratio 2: \(\dfrac{ 4 }{ 9 } : \dfrac{ 8 }{ 97 }\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. Find the LCD of 9 and 97.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \text{LCD} = 97
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Convert \(\dfrac{ 4 }{ 9 }\) to an equivalent fraction with the LCD as the denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \dfrac{ 4 }{ 9 } = \dfrac{ 4 \times 10 }{ 9 \times 10 } = \dfrac{ 40 }{ 90 }
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. Now we have:
