[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 5:  Simplifying further, we see that the entire statement is, $\frac{7}{1} = \frac{8}{7} \Rightarrow \frac{7 \cdot 7}{1} = \frac{8 \cdot 8}{7} \Rightarrow7 \cdot 7 = 8 \cdot 8$, and we are given $7! = 1! \cdot 7! = 0! \cdot 7! = 1 \cdot 7!$ and $8! = 1! \cdot 8! = 1 \cdot 8! = 1 \cdot 8!$, so the last equation $8 \cdot 8 = 1 \cdot 8!$ doesn't surprise us as it makes sense.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 6:  Hence, the first term $x = \frac{7}{1}.
