[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Points $X$ and $Y$ lie on sides $AB$ and $AC$ respectively of triangle $ABC$. If $AB=7$, $AC=10$, $AX=4$ and $AY=6$, what is the ratio of the area of triangle $AXY$ to the area of triangle $ABC$?
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \C+=
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Since $AX = 4$, we can infer that $x\_1 = 4$, $x\_2 = 4 + 1 = 5$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Similarly, since $AY = 6$, we can infer that $x\_3 = 6$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Using the formula for the area of a triangle, we have
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \frac{1}{2} \times AB \times x\_1 (\overline{i}) - \frac{1}{2} \times AC \times x\_2 (\overline{j}) = \frac{1}{2} \times AX \times x\_3 (\overline{k})
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m which simplifies to
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m AB - AC = AX + y \cdot x\_2 (\overline{k})
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m where $y$ is the length of $\overline{BC}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Given that $AB = 7$, $AC = 10$, and $AX = 4$ and $AY=6$, we can solve for $y$:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 10 - 7 = 4 + y \cdot 6 \Rightarrow y = 6
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, the ratio of the area of triangle $AXY$ to the area of triangle $ABC$ is $9/10$.<|endoftext|>
