[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Find the volume of the tetrahedron whose vertices are $A = (0,1,2),$ $B = (3,0,1),$ $C = (4,3,6),$ and $D = (2,3,2).$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the volume of the tetrahedron with vertices \(A = (0,1,2)\), \(B = (3,0,1)\), \(C = (4,3,6)\), and \(D = (2,3,2)\), we can use the formula for the volume of a tetrahedron with vertices given in space:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m V = \frac{1}{6} \left| \det(A, B, C, D) \right|
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Here, \(A = (0,1,2)\), \(B = (3,0,1)\), \(C = (4,3,6)\), and \(D = (2,3,2)\). We first identify the matrix \(\det(A, B, C, D)\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \det \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3 & 0 & 4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 0 & 3 & 3 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1 & 1 & 2
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the determinant, we expand along the first row:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \det \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3 & 0 & 4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 0 & 3 & 3 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1 & 1 & 2
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{pmatrix} = 3 \det \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3 & 3 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1 & 2
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{pmatrix} - 0 \cdot \det \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 0 & 3 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1 & 2
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{pmatrix} + 4 \det \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 0 & 3 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1 & 1
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The minors are:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \det \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3 & 3 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1 & 2
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{pmatrix} = 3 \cdot 2 - 3 \cdot 1 = 6 - 3 = 3
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m And the determinant of the entire matrix is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \det \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3 & 3 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1 & 2
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{pmatrix} = 3 \cdot 2 - 3 \cdot 1 = 6 - 3 = 3
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, the determinant is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3 \cdot 3 + 0 \cdot (3 \cdot 2 - 3 \cdot 1) + 4 \cdot 0 \cdot (0 \cdot 1 - 3 \cdot 1) = 9 + 0 + 0 = 9
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now we can find the volume \(V\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m V = \frac{1}{6} \left| 9 \right| = \frac{1}{6} \cdot 9 = \frac{9}{6} = \frac{3}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, the volume of the tetrahedron is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \boxed{\frac{3}{2}}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
