[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The projection of a vector \begin{pmatrix} \text{x} \\ \text{y} \end{pmatrix} is given by the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \text{proj}_{\begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \end{pmatrix}} \begin{pmatrix} \text{x} \\ \text{y} \end{pmatrix} &= \frac{\begin{pmatrix} \text{x} \\ \text{y} \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \end{pmatrix}}{\begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \end{pmatrix}} \times \begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Then, the projection of \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix} onto \begin{pmatrix} 8 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 8 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} &= 4 != 8 \\ \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 8 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} / 8 \cdot 8 + 1 \cdot 1 = (\text{between -}\sqrt{65} \text{ and -1} \text{), } -\frac{\sqrt{65}}{16}. \end{align}<|endoftext|>
