[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Calculate the g-Value, required by Gordon:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ G-F=\frac{b(r_{1,n}-b(r_{2,n})-(r_{1,n}-r_{2,n})\frac{\Delta \sigma_{n,{C,G}}}{P_{n}})}{d(r_{2,n}^(1)+r_{2,n}^(2) )-r_{2,n}} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Select the correct answer within parentheses.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To calculate the required g-value (G-F) using the Gordon inequality for a bond, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. Determine the values of \( r_{1,0} \), \( b(r_{1,0}) \), \( r_{2,0} \), \( b(r_{2,0}) \), \( r_{1,N} \), \( r_{1,N,m-n} \), \( r_{2,N} \), \( J \), \( t_{1,N} \), and \( t_{2,N} \) based on the given information.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Convert the redemption values from floating to flat denominator on the right side of the inequality.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. Calculate the midpoint values between the given values.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4. Substitute the calculated values into the Gordon inequality formula and perform the necessary calculations.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let's start with the given information:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \( r_{1,0} = 0.07 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \( b(r_{1,0}) = \frac{r_{1,0}}{1 + r_{1,0}} \)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \( r_{2,0} = 0.08 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \( b(r_{2,0}) = \frac{r_{2,0}}{1 + r_{2,0}} \)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \( r_{1,N} = 0.06 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \( r_{1,N,m-n} = \frac{r_{1,N} + r_{1,N + m - n} - r_{1,N} \times t_{1,N}}{\frac{1}{r_{2,0} + r_{2,N}}} \)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \( r_{2,N} = \frac{r_{2,0} - r_{2,N} - t_{1,N} \times J}{\frac{1}{r_{2,1}^{{}} + r_{2,2}^{{}}} - t_{1,N} \times J} \)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \( J = \frac{0.002 \times 0.06 + 0.002 \times 0.08}{7.92 \times 12} = 0.02 \)
