[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \( t_{2,N} = \frac{0.013 + 0.02}{(0.06)} = 0.1857 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, let's calculate the midpoint values between the given values:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \( t_{1,0} = 0 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \( t_{1,m-n} = t_{1,N,m-n} = t_{1,N} - r_{2,N} = r_{1,0} = 0.07 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \( t_{1,m-n + n} = t_{1,N,m-n + n} = t_{1,N} + r_{2,N} = 0.07 + 0.08 = 0.05 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
