[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \( t_{2,m-n} = t_{2,N,m-n} = t_{2,N} - r_{1,N} = 0.06 - 0.05 = 0.01 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \( t_{2,m-n + n} = t_{2,N,m-n + n} = t_{2,N} + r_{1,N} = 0.06 + 0.05 = 0.01 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Finally, we can substitute these values into the Gordon inequality formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ G-F = \frac{b(r_{1,0}, b(r_{1,0}), r_{2,0}, b(r_{2,0}), r_{1,N}, r_{1,N,m-n}, r_{2,N}, J, t_{1,N})}{d(r_{2,N}^{\left(1\right)} + r_{2,N}^{\left(2\right)}) - r_{2,N}} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
