[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 1:First, we need to calculate the angle we are integrating (let's call it $\theta$).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  theta = 240^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 2: Since $\theta$ is in the fourth quadrant, we can convert it using the conversion formula, $\theta = 180^\circ - A \times \frac{3}{2}$ where $A$ is the angle in degrees. In our case, $A = 240^\circ$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  theta = 180^\circ - (240^\circ \times \frac{3}{2}) = 180^\circ - 360^\circ = -180^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 3: Now that we have the angle in degrees, we can calculate $\tan(\theta)$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  \sin(\theta) &= \sin(-180^\circ) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  \cos(\theta) &= \cos(-180^\circ) \\\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  \tan(\theta) &= \frac{\sin(\theta)}{\cos(\theta)} \\\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  &= \frac{\sin(-180^\circ)}{\cos(-180^\circ)}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 4: We realize that $\sin(-180^\circ) = -\sin(180^\circ) = -1$ and $\cos(-180^\circ) = \cos(180^\circ) = -1$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  \tan(\theta) &= \frac{-\sin(180^\circ)}{\cos(180^\circ)} \\\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  &= \frac{-(-1)}{(-1)} \\\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  &= \frac{1}{-1} \\\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  &= -1
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  \end{align*}
