[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let $\mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 4 \\ 6 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\mathbf{c} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -7 \\ -10 \end{pmatrix}.$  Find the maximum value of
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[\mathbf{c} \cdot (\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}),\]where $\mathbf{a}$ is a unit vector.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \mathbf{c} \cdot (\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}) &= \overrightarrow{a} \cdot \left(((\mathbf{a}-\mathbf{b})\mathbf{i}) \times (\mathbf{a}-\mathbf{b})\right) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= \overrightarrow{a} \cdot \left(-(\mathbf{a}-\mathbf{b})\right) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= -\left(\mathbf{a}\cdot(\mathbf{a}-\mathbf{b}) + \mathbf{b}\cdot(\mathbf{a}-\mathbf{b})\right) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= -\left(\mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{a} - \mathbf{a}\cdot\mathbf{b} + \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{a} - \mathbf{b}\cdot\mathbf{b}\right) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= -\left(\mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{a} - \mathbf{a}\cdot\mathbf{b} + \mathbf{b}\cdot\mathbf{a}\right) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= -\left(\|\mathbf{a}\|^2 - \mathbf{a}\cdot\mathbf{b}\right) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= -\left(\|\mathbf{a}\|^2 - \frac{\|(\mathbf{a},\mathbf{b})\|^2}{2} \right) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= -\frac{2}{2} \|\mathbf{a}\|^2 - \operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{b}} (\mathbf{a})\cdot\mathbf{a} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, compare the squared Euclidean norms of $\mathbf{a}$ with the ratio of its projection multiplied by $\mathbf{b}$ to find the condition that $p$ must satisfy.<|endoftext|>
