[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4. Substituting these into the sum equation, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    b + (b + d) + (b + 2d) + (b + 3d) + (b + 4d) = 360^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 5. Simplifying the left side of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    5b + 10d = 360^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 6. We also have the condition that \(v, w, x, y, z\) form an arithmetic sequence. This means that the difference between consecutive terms is constant:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    w - v = x - w = y - x = z - y
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 7. From the arithmetic sequence condition, we know that:
