[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The mean of the set of numbers $\{87,85,80,83,84,x\}$ is 83.5. What is the median of the set of six numbers? Express your answer as a decimal to the nearest tenth.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To solve this problem, we need to find the value of \( x \) that makes the mean of the set of numbers \(\{87, 85, 80, 83, 84, x\}\) equal to 83.5.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m First, we calculate the sum of the given numbers:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 87 + 85 + 80 + 83 + 84 + x
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Adding these together:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 87 + 85 = 172
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 172 + 80 = 252
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 252 + 83 = 335
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 335 + 84 = 419
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, the sum of all the numbers was 419.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Since the mean is 83.5:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \text{Mean} = \frac{\text{Sum of the numbers}}{\text{Number of numbers}} = 83.5
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m For a set of six numbers to have a mean of 83.5, the sum of the numbers must be \(\text{Mean} \times 6\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 419 = 83.5 \times 6
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Since we found that, this equation holds true, it confirms that the mean equals 83.5, meaning the value of \( x \) cannot be determined from the given information alone.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Thus, the median of the set of six numbers, given that the mean of the set of numbers \(\{87, 85, 80, 83, 84, x\}\) is 83.5, is not unique. 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Since \( x \) is not specified, one possible number for \( x \) that meets the criteria is 82.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, the median is \( 82 \), or \boxed{82.0}.<|endoftext|>
