[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$(4\sqrt{(x^2 + y^2)} + 3.5\sqrt{(x^2 + y^2)}) - 0'$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\text{length of side } AB:\sqrt{(4\sqrt{(0^2 + 7^2)} + 3.5\sqrt{(0^2 + 7^2)})}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\text{length of side } BC:\sqrt{(4\sqrt((-1)^2 + 6^2)}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\text{length of side } CA:\sqrt{(4\sqrt((-4)^2 + 9^2)}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, we need to find the length of the third side using the distance formula:  $\sqrt{(4\sqrt{(0^2 + 7^2)} + 3.5\sqrt{(0^2 + 7^2)})^2 + 0^2 + 5^2 - (-1)^2 + 6^2 - 0^2 + 1^2}$
