[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m An exponent with a negative exponent "(" : "^[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We can rewrite $32^5$ as $(2^5)^5$, and we can write $\left \lfloor\frac{1}{(2^5)^5}\right \rfloor = \left \lfloor \frac{1}{32^5}\right \rfloor = \frac{1}{32^5} = 64^{-5}$ because $\left \lfloor x+y \right \rfloor = \left \lfloor x \right \rfloor + \text{integer part of}~ y$.<|endoftext|>
