[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The $y$-intercept occurs when we set $x=0,$ so it is $(0,0).$ The slope $-2$ yanks the line upward, so the distance between the $y$-intercept and the $x$-intercept is the same distance as the absolute value of the slope multiplied by the $x$-intercept distance, so it's $(2 \cdot 5) = \boxed{10}.$<|endoftext|>
