[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - 3/7/2017\n/ox89UU\nhow can i find which of my google account links are authorized to use my passwordlets
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To determine which Google account links are authorized to use your passwordlets, follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. **Identify Your Account:**
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - Note down the device IDs of your Google accounts. For example, if you have two Google accounts using Two-Factor Authentication (2FA) with Google Authenticator apps, these IDs are typically marked as “Google Account.”
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. **Check for App Access Controls:**
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - Open the Google Store and search for "Google Authenticator" app filters.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - Look for apps that support the Current Authentication Model. This can be found in the Apps tab within the Google Store.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. **Look for Authorized Passwordlets:**
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - On the text view (term settings) of the apps, select the three dots to expand it.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - Next to each authorized app, check the box next to **Supports Two-Factor Authentication (2FA)**. If this option is dark gray or not selected, some apps do not support 2FA.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4. **Confirm Authorization:**
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - Check if all apps listed in the authorized filters start with light-colored circles. Click on these apps again.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - Verify that all apps are listed with a green checkmark and that they all use 2FA.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 5. **Manual Check:**
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - If you need to confirm manually, use the Google Assistant to ask "Is this an authorized Google account?" Yes, if all devices show this phrase.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 6. **Test with Specific Apps:**
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - Test a single device with all authorized apps and see if they work correctly.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ### Example for iPhones:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - Apple provides support for various Google account devices (Mac, iPhone, iPad, iPod Touch, etc.).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - On your iPhone, go to **Settings** > **Apple ID** > **Authentication** > Touch ID & PIN > Secure Access.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - Click **Pay For App** and **Use on my Device** to secure your app if required.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ### Example for Android Phones:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - Google initially supported Android devices (Android Wear Edition subscription supported Google Services for 5 years).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - On your Android device, you can use an option panel near the menu.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - Look for services package where Google Services are installed.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - Access your Google account and click **two-factor authentication**.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m By following these steps, you should be able to determine which of your Google account links are authorized to use your passwordlets.<|endoftext|>
