[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the value of \( k \) that makes the volume of the parallelepiped generated by the vectors \(\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix},\) \(\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ k \\ 2 \end{pmatrix},\) and \(\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \\ k \end{pmatrix}\) equal to 15, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. **Calculate the area of the base:**
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    The base of the parallelepiped is a triangle formed by the three vectors. The area of this triangle can be found using the cross product of two of the vectors and the magnitude of the third vector.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    Let \(\vec{A} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\vec{B} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ k \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}\). We need to find \(\vec{C} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \\ k \end{pmatrix}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    The vectors \(\vec{C}\) and \(\vec{B}\) form the sides of the triangle:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \vec{B} \times \vec{C} = \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \vec{i} & \vec{j} & \vec{k} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    1 & k & 2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    1 & 2 & k
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    Calculating the determinant:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \vec{B} \times \vec{C} = \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    k & 2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    2 & k
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \end{vmatrix} = (k \cdot k) - (2 \cdot 2) = k^2 - 4
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    So, the area \( A \) of the base is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    A = \frac{1}{2} \cdot \text{base area} = \frac{1}{2} \cdot |k^2 - 4|
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. **Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped:**
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    The volume \( V \) of the parallelepiped is the area of the base times the height \( h \):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    V = A \cdot h
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    We know \( V = 15 \), so:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    15 = \frac{1}{2} \cdot |k^2 - 4| \cdot h
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    Solving for \( |k^2 - 4| \):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \frac{30}{|k^2 - 4|} = h
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. **Determine the height \( h \):**
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    The height \( h \) of the parallelepiped is the perpendicular distance between the planes of the three vectors \(\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix},\) \(\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ k \\ 2 \end{pmatrix},\) and \(\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \\ k \end{pmatrix}\). This can be found using the cross product of two vectors and the determinant method of volume:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    h = \frac{\begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \vec{x} & \vec{y} & \vec{z} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    2 & 3 & 4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    1 & k & 2
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \end{vmatrix}}{\begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \vec{x} & \vec{y} & \vec{z} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \vec{a} & \vec{b} & \vec{c}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \end{vmatrix}}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    Let's denote the vectors as:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \vec{x} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}, \quad \vec{y} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ k \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}, \quad \vec{z} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \\ k \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    Then:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    h = \frac{\begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \vec{2} & \vec{3} & \vec{4} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    1 & k & 2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    k & 1 & k
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \end{vmatrix}}{\begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    2 & 3 & 4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    1 & k & 2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    k & 1 & k
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \end{vmatrix}}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    Calculating the determinants:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    2 & 3 & 4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    1 & k & 2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    k & 1 & k
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \end{vmatrix} = 2 \cdot (k \cdot k - 1 \cdot 1) - 3 \cdot (1 \cdot k - 2 \cdot k) + 4 \cdot (1 \cdot 1 - k \cdot k)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    Simplifying:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    = 2(k^2 - 1) - 3(k - 2k) + 4(1 - k^2) = 2k^2 - 2 - 3k + 6 - 4 + 4k^2
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
