[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The sign function $\text{sgn}(x)$ is defined by \[\text{sgn}(x) = \left\{ \begin{aligned} -1 \quad &\text{if } x < 0 \\ 0 \quad &\text{if } x = 0 \\ 1 \quad &\text{if } x > 0. \end{aligned} \right. \]Compute $\sum_{n=-10}^{20} \text{sgn}(n).$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To compute the sum \sum_{n=-10}^{20} \text{sgn}(n), we need to count how many times the sign function \text{sgn}(n) equals 1. First, let's identify when \text{sgn}(n) equals 1. If \( n \neq 0 \), then \text{sgn}(n) = 1. If \( n = 0 \), then \text{sgn}(0) = 0, which is not necessary to consider in this equation. Therefore, we only need to consider \( n \neq 0 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Rewrite the equation \text{sgn}(n) = 1 as \( n \neq 0 \). Now, we need to count how many such \( n \) are in the range \([-10, 20]\). Since \( n \) ranges from \(-10\) to \(20\), we subtract 1 from each endpoint to get the correct range. This means \( n \) ranges from \(-10\) to \(19\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, we need to count the numbers between \(-10\) and \(19\) that are not equal to 0. The steps are as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. From \(-10\) to \(19\), the difference is \(19 - (-10) + 1 = 20\). This means the numbers range from \(-10\) to \(19\), inclusive of \(-10\) but excluding 10 and 20.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. There are \(21\) numbers from \(-10\) to \(19\) in total. We need to exclude 10 and 20 because they are not in the set \(\{-10, -9, \ldots, 19\}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, the count of numbers \( n = -10, -9, \ldots, 20 \) is \(-10 - (-1) = -10 + 1 = -9\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, \sum_{n=-10}^{20} \text{sgn}(n) = -9\). The final answer is \(\boxed{-9}\).<|endoftext|>
