[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m In order to solve the given equation \[\frac{x^2+11x+28}{x+4} - 7 = x,\] follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. Simplify and rearrange the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[\frac{x^2+11x+28}{x+4} - 7 = x.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Subtract 7 from both sides to isolate the fraction on one side of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[\frac{x^2+11x+28}{x+4} = x + 7.\] 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. Multiply both sides by the denominator of \(x + 4\) to eliminate the denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[(x^2+11x+28) = (x + 4)(x + 7).\] 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4. Expand the right side of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[(x^2+11x+28) = x^2 + 11x + 28.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 5. Subtract \(x^2 + 11x + 28\) from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[-28 = 0.\] 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 6. Simplify to solve for \(x\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[\boxed{x = \boxed{0}.\]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
