[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m In 2004, Marika's father was \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 8 \cdot 4 + 4 = 36
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \] years old. In an extra year, when Marika's father will be 36, \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 9 = 8 + 3 = 8 + (11 - 8 + 8) - 8 = 8 + (11 - (8 + 8)) - 8 + 8 = 8 + 8 = 12
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \] years old. Here, we have used the average A+TEKI equation, which states that when an equation like the one this problem presents involves the sum of two terms, the difference between the ages of the two persons, and the product of the two ages, the ages of the two persons can be calculated by substituting the given age pairs into the equation.
