[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 5 red plates + 4 blue plates = 9 plates in total.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The number of ways to choose 2 plates out of 9 is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m {/eq}C(9, 2) = 9C2 = 9 x 8 / 2 = 36.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m {/eq}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, we need to find out the number of ways to choose 2 plates that are of different colors. 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m {/eq} {eq}There are 5 red plates * (5 - 1) = 5 red plates * 4 = 20 red plates.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m {/eq} remaining plates, 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m and there are 4 blue plates * (4-1) = 4 blue plates * 3 = 12 blue plates.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m {/eq}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The number of ways to choose 2 plates out of those is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m {/eq}C(20, 2) + C(12, 2) = (20 * 19) + (12 * 11) = 380 (red plates) + 132 (blue plates) = 512.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m {/eq}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, the number of ways to choose 2 plates of the same color is 512. 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m {/eq}
