[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Start by finding the volume of each individual box. The volume of a cube is calculated using the formula: Volume = edge length^3. So the volume of the first box is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  Volume1 = (4 feet)^3
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  64 cubic feet.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 	
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Similarly, calculate the volume for the second box:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  Volume2 = (4 feet)^3
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  64 cubic feet.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 	
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Finally, to get the total volume, add the volumes to one another:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  Total volume = Volume1 + Volume2
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  64 cubic feet.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Next, it's easy to find the total volume of all three boxes. You will get:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  Total volume = Volume1 + Volume2 + Volume3 = 64 cubic feet + 64 cubic feet + 64 cubic feet = 192 cubic feet.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <decimalsvolume=volume1 + volume2 + total volume
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <decimalsvolume = 192
