[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We are given that $\overline{AB} \| \overline{CD}$ $\overline{AD}$ is a diameter of the circle and $AD = 36^{circ}$. To find the length of $\overline{AB}$ in inches, we need to find the radius of the circle, as the length of the chord $\overline{AB} = 2r$, and $\overline{AB} = \frac{36}{2}r$. Thus, the length of $\overline{AB}$ is: \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \overline{AB} &= \frac{36}{2} \cdot \pi \cdot r \\[6pt]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= 18 \cdot \pi \cdot r
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*} The radius of the circle can be found from $\frac{36\pi}{2} = \pi$, giving a radius of 54 inches. Finally, the length of $\overline{AB}$ in inches is: \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \boxed{81\pi}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}<|endoftext|>
