[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m     - The right side: \(1 = 1\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The equations hold true for \(n=0\). Therefore, \(a_0 = -2\) and \(b_0 = 1\) hold true.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 3: Find \(a_{2012}\) and \(b_{2012}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m a. Using the equations, we can find \(a_{2012}\) and \(b_{2012}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m     - From the first equation, \(a_{2012} = a_0 + b_0 + \sqrt{a_0^2 + b_0^2} = -2 + 1 + \sqrt{(-2)^2 + 1^2} = -1 + \sqrt{4 + 1} = -1 + \sqrt{5} = -1 + \sqrt{2010}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m     - Similarly,
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m     - From the second equation, \(b_{2012} = a_0 + b_0 - \sqrt{a_0^2 + b_0^2} = -2 + 1 - \sqrt{(-2)^2 + 1^2} = -1 - \sqrt{4 + 1} = -1 - \sqrt{5} = -1 - \sqrt{2010}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
