[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m If $x + \frac{1}{x} = 5,$ then compute the value of
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[(x - 2)^2 + \frac{25}{(x - 2)^2}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Since \begin{align*}x + \frac{1}{x} = 5\end{align*}, you have \begin{equation}x^2 + 1 = 6\end{equation} by factoring. That is, \begin{align*}x^2 + 1 &= 6\\ x^2 &= 5 \\ x &= \pm \sqrt{5}\end{align*} From \begin{equation}\frac{25}{x^2} = \frac{5}{x^2} < 1\end{equation}. Thus, \begin{equation}\frac{25}{(x - 2)^2} < 1.\end{equation} Therefore, \begin{gather*}x - 2 < 1.1 \\ x < 3.1\end{gather*}Seems reasonable until you reach \begin{equation}x - 2 = - \sqrt{5}\end{equation}, \begin{align*} -\sqrt{5} = \sqrt{5} \cdot -1\end{align*}, \begin{align*}x = - 2 \sqrt 5 \,\,\,\,\, \Longrightarrow (x - 2)^2 + \frac 25\\ = -4 \sqrt 5 + \frac 25 \,\,\,\,\, < \quad  \boxed{ 7 / 5}\end{equation}
