[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Certainly! To find the volume of a pyramid whose base is one face of a cube of side length 2 and whose apex is the center of the cube, we can use the formula for the volume of a pyramid, which is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ V = \frac{1}{3} \times \text{Base Area} \times \text{ Height} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m First, determine the area of the base:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - The base is a square with side length 2.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - Area of the base = \(2 \times 2 = 4\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Next, find the height of the pyramid. The height of the pyramid is the perpendicular distance from the center of the base to the apex of the pyramid.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The center of the base (one vertex) is the midpoint of the diagonal of the base (since the base is a square and the apex is the center inside the cube), so the height (o) is half the side length of the base.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ o = \frac{2}{2} = 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, we can substitute these values into the volume formula.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ V = \frac{1}{3} \times 4 \times 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ V = \frac{4}{3} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So the volume of the pyramid is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ \boxed{\frac{4}{3}} \]<|endoftext|>
