[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Determine the number of ways to arrange the letters of the word TARTAR.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To determine the number of ways to arrange the letters of the word "TARTAR," we will use the formula for permutations of a multiset. The word "TARTAR" consists of 4 letters where 'T' appears twice and 'A' and 'R' appear once each. The formula for permuting a multiset is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \text{Number of permutations} = \frac{n!}{n_1! \times n_2! \times \cdots \times n_k!}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m where:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \( n \) is the total number of items,
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \( n_1, n_2, \ldots, n_k \) are the frequencies of the distinct items.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m For the word "TARTAR":
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \( n = 4 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \( n_1 = 2 \) (for 'T').
