[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So we need to calculate:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \text{Number of permutations} = \frac{4!}{2! \times 1! \times 1!}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m First, calculate the factorials:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4! = 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1 = 24
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2! = 2 \times 1 = 2
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1! = 1 \times 1 = 1
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now substitute these values back into the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \text{Number of permutations} = \frac{24}{2 \times 1 \times 1} = \frac{24}{2} = 12
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Thus, the number of ways to arrange the letters of the word "TARTAR" is \(\boxed{12}\).<|endoftext|>
