[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The way to approach the problem is to first write down the congruence to find the quotients.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\log_{10}{28471}\ \equiv\ \text{quotient}_1\ \pmod{\text{lcm}(2,5)}\\ \text{quotient}_1\ \equiv\ \text{quotient}_2\ \pmod{\text{lcm}(2,7)}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To simplify the left side, we can write:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\log_{10}{28471}\ \equiv\ \text{quotient}_1\ \pmod{(25,5,7)}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We want to find the quotient between 3 and 4.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The calculations for $\log_{10}{28471}/3$ and $\log_{10}{28471}/4$ are straightforward.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\begin{aligned}\log_{10}{28471}/3\ \&\log_{10}{28471}/4\\ \log_{10}{28471}/3\ \&\log_{10}{28471}/4 &= 28471/16816\\ &=10/4 \end{aligned}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Expressing the results in base 10 we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\begin{aligned}-2\log_{10}{28471}/10 &\equiv 10/4\ (befor \酴\\[-10pt] -(10/4)/(25/7)\ (after \酴)\\ &= -10/4\cdot28471/125\\ &=-28470/500\ (by \.INVISIBLE \LEFTSHIFT 1\Russian \RIGHTSHIFT)\\ &=-569个角 attention!\end{aligned}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m What needs to be done, is choosing the appropriate base that the numbers are divided by. We have:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$-569\cdot-28470\div-569\cdot10\div-569\cdot4$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m This all turns out to be:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$-569(-28470)div10div10div4$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m This final multiplication shows that the sum of the quotients is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$-569(-28470)div10div10div4=\{}$$<|endoftext|>
