[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m At the beginning of the day, Margaret had 72 ice cream cones. By noon, she had $\frac{2}{3}$ as many cones as she had at the beginning of the day, which is $\frac{2}{3} \times 72 = 48$ cones.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m By the end of the day, she had $\frac{2}{3}$ as many cones as she had at noon, which is $\frac{2}{3} \times 48 = 32$ cones.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, the ice cream cones Margaret has at the end of the day are \boxed{32}.<|endoftext|>
