[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Sure thing! Let's break down the problem into smaller parts. When we flip each coin 1/several times and observe either heads or tails, there are three possible outcomes and 3^3 possible combinations. So we have 3 possible outcomes and 3^3 = 27 possible outcomes.
