[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 1:   From the ratio, there are 4 parts for female students. If there are 396 female students, then the number of other students can be calculated as:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Number of other students = 9/4 * 396 = 837
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 2:  Since there are 1 parts for teachers, then the total number of teachers will be 11 parts. The total number of students will be the sum of all the sum of the number of teachers, other students, and females:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Total number of students = 11 * (396 + 837) = 504
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 3:  The ratio of teachers to students is 1 to 11 (11 parts). Therefore, the number of teachers will be:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Number of teachers = 11/11 * 504 = 504
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Wrapping everything up, the number of teachers in the given school is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \boxed{504}<|endoftext|>
