[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m First, we need to determine the general form of the equation since we know the curve is a parabola, we can use this to find the constant and coefficients of the equation.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Then, we use the point-slope form of a line to find the coordinates of the vertex and the equation of the side of the equation.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The standard form to parabola is $y = ax^2 + bx + c$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We know from practice that the slope of the sides of the parabola is determined by the derivative of the center x-coordinate.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, for $x = u = 2t + 5$, substituting into the general form, we get $y = 2a(u)^2 + bu + c = 2a(2t + 5)^2 + 12t^2 - 20t - 20$.
