[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Find the ordered pair $(x,y)$ if
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m x+y&=(3-x)+(3-y),\\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m x-y &=(x-2)+(y-2).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To solve the given system of linear equations, we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. Identify the system of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    x + y &= 3 - x + 3 - y \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    x - y &= x - 2 + y - 2
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Simplify the equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    x + y &= 6 - x + 3 - y \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    x - y &= x + y - 4
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. Combine like terms and simplify each equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    x + y + y &= 6 + 3 - 4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    x + 2y &= 5
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    And for the second equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    x + y - y &= x - 4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    x - 4 &= x - 4
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4. The simplified form of the system of equations is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    x + 2y &= 5 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    x - 4 &= x - 4 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 5. Add the two equations to eliminate \(x\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    x + 2y + x - 4 &= 5 + (x - 4) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    2x + 2y - 4 &= 5 + x - 4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    2x + 2y - 4 &= x + 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    x + 2y - 4 &= 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    x + 2y &= 5
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 6. Solve for \(y\) in terms of \(x\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    x + 2y &= 5 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    2y &= 5 - x \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    y &= \frac{5 - x}{2} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    y &= \frac{x + 5}{2} 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    To apply the same method to the second equation, we should reverse our steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    1. Invert the second equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      (x - 4) = x - 4 \implies x - 4 + 4 = x - 4 + 4 \implies x = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    2. Substitute this \(x\) value back into the first equation to find \(y\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      0 + y &= 6 - 0 + 3 - y \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      y &= 9 - 2y
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      0 + 2y &= 9 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      y &= 9
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    So the solution pair \((x, y)\) is \((0, 9)\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
