[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let $\mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 4 \\ 6 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\mathbf{c} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -7 \\ -10 \end{pmatrix}.$  Find the maximum value of
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[\mathbf{c} \cdot (\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}),\]where $\mathbf{a}$ is a unit vector.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the maximum value of \(\mathbf{c} \cdot (\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b})\), we will proceed through systematic methods.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 4 \\ 6 \end{pmatrix} \quad \text{and} \quad \mathbf{c} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -7 \\ -10 \end{pmatrix}, \quad \text{and} \quad \mathbf{a} \text{ is a unit vector.}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ### Step 1: Calculate \(\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We need to find the cross product \(\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}\). Since \(\mathbf{a}\) is a unit vector, \(\|\mathbf{a}\| = 1\). The cross product \(\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b} = \| \mathbf{a} \| \, \mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{a} = \begin{vmatrix} \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\ a_1 & a_2 & a_3 \\ a_1 & a_2 & a_3 \end{vmatrix} = (a_2 a_3 - a_3 a_2) \mathbf{i} - (a_1 a_3 - a_3 a_1) \mathbf{j} + (a_1 a_2 - a_2 a_1) \mathbf{k}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Substituting the values from \(\mathbf{b}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b} = (-1 \cdot 4 - 6 \cdot 2) \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -7 \\ -10 \end{pmatrix} - (-1 \cdot -10 - 6 \cdot 2) \begin{pmatrix} -7 \\ -10 \\ 6 \end{pmatrix} + (2 \cdot -7 - (-7) \cdot 4) \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -10 \\ 6 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m = (-4 - 12) \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -7 \\ -10 \end{pmatrix} - (10 - 12) \begin{pmatrix} -7 \\ -10 \\ 6 \end{pmatrix} + (-14 + 28) \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -10 \\ 6 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m = -16 \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -7 \\ -10 \end{pmatrix} + 2 \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ 10 \\ -6 \end{pmatrix} + 14 \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -10 \\ 6 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m = \begin{pmatrix} -32 \\ 112 \\ 160 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} 14 \\ 20 \\ -12 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} 28 \\ -140 \\ 84 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m = \begin{pmatrix} -32 + 14 + 28 \\ 112 + 20 + -140 \\ 160 - 12 + 84 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \\ 242 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ### Step 2: Calculate \(\mathbf{c} \cdot \mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, we need to calculate \(\mathbf{c} \cdot (\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b})\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \mathbf{c} \cdot \mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b} = 6 \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -7 \\ -10 \end{pmatrix} - 2 \begin{pmatrix} 14 \\ 20 \\ -12 \end{pmatrix} + 28 \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -10 \\ 6 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m = \begin{pmatrix} 12 \\ -42 \\ -60 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 28 \\ -40 \\ -24 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} 56 \\ -200 \\ 168 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m = \begin{pmatrix} 12 - 28 + 56 \\ -42 + 40 - 200 + 168 \\ -60 - 24 + 168 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 40 \\ 4 \\ 84 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ### Step 3: Find the maximum value
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The maximum value of \(\mathbf{c} \cdot (\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b})\) is the magnitude of \(\mathbf{40} + 4 + 84 = 98\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Thus, the maximum value of \(\mathbf{c} \cdot (\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b})\) is \(\boxed{98}\).<|endoftext|>
