[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find \(\mathbf{A} + 8 \mathbf{A}^{-1}\), we start with the given equation \((\mathbf{A} - 2 \mathbf{I})(\mathbf{A} - 4 \mathbf{I}) = \mathbf{0}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m First, let's expand the left-hand side of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m (\mathbf{A} - 2 \mathbf{I})(\mathbf{A} - 4 \mathbf{I}).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Using the distributive property of matrix multiplication, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \mathbf{A} \mathbf{A} - 4 \mathbf{A} \mathbf{I} - 2 \mathbf{I} \mathbf{A} + 8 \mathbf{I} \mathbf{I}.
