[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Since \(\mathbf{I} \mathbf{A}\) and \(\mathbf{I} \mathbf{I}\) are scalars and there are no other non-zero entries, we can simplify this to:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \mathbf{A}^2 - 6 \mathbf{A} + 8 \mathbf{I},
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m where \(\mathbf{I}\) is the identity matrix. Thus, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m (\mathbf{A} - 2 \mathbf{I})(\mathbf{A} - 4 \mathbf{I}) = \mathbf{A}^2 - 6 \mathbf{A} + 8 \mathbf{I}.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Given that this expression equals the zero matrix \(\mathbf{0}\), we can write:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
