[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m A man nearing retirement wants to invest some money in a fund that compounds annually at a rate of 6 percent, so that in five years, he will have at least $\$100,000$.  How much money must he invest now to make that happen?  (Give your answer to the nearest dollar.)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the initial investment required from an account that compounds annually at 6%, we can use the compound interest formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ```
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m A = P(1 + r/n)^(nt)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ```
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Where:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - A is the amount of money accumulated after n years, including interest.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - P is the principal amount (the initial amount of money).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - r is the annual interest rate (decimal).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - n is the number of times that interest is compounded per year.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - t is the time the money is invested for in years.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - A = \$100,000
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - r = 0.06
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - n = 1 (since the interest is compounded annually)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - t = 5 (since this is two years, we need 5 years of investments)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We need to solve for P:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ```
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 100000 = P(1 + 0.06/1)^(1*5)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ```
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Simplifying, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ```
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 100000 = P(1 + 0.06)^5
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ```
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, take the fifth root of both sides to isolate P:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ```
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m P = \frac{100000}{(1 + 0.06)^5}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ```
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
