[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We need to calculate the dilation centered at $-1 + 4i$ with a scale factor of $-2$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m This means we need to calculate the new complex number $-2 \cdot (-1 + 4i)$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To do this, we can multiply $-1 + 4i$ by $-2$ and simplify.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m (-1 + 4i) \cdot (-2) &= 2 + 8i \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The resulting complex number is $2 + 8i$, so the dilation takes $2i$ to $\boxed{2 + 8i}$.
