[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To solve this problem, we can start by setting up an equation from the given information.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let the original number be \( x \). According to the given problem, when the number \( x \) is multiplied by 5, it equals 21 plus twice the original number. So, we can write:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ 5x = 21 + 2x \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Next, we need to isolate \( x \) by moving all terms involving \( x \) to one side of the equation and constant terms to the other side. We can do this by subtracting \( 2x \) from both sides of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ 5x - 2x = 21 + 2x - 2x \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ 3x = 21 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, we can solve for \( x \) by dividing both sides of the equation by 3:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ \frac{3x}{3} = \frac{21}{3} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ x = 7 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, the value of the original number is 7:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \boxed{7}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
