[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m What is the value of \[\frac{x^1\cdot x^2\cdot x^3\cdots x^9}{x^2\cdot x^4 \cdot x^6 \cdots x^{12}}\]if $x=5$?
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Hello, user! I will solve the expression step by step below.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\dfrac{x^{1}\cdot x^{2}\cdot x^{3}\cdots x^{9}}{x^{2}\cdot x^{4 \cdot} \cdot x^{6 \cdot} \cdot \cdots x^{12 \cdot}}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m By simplifying the exponent on the denominator, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\dfrac{x^{1+2+3+\cdots+9}}{x^{2+4+6+\cdots+12}}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Combining the summation terms on the exponents, we obtain:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\dfrac{x^{21}}{x^{21}}$$
