[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To calculate the value of the expression ∫_0^1 9x^(2x) dx, we need to know the value of x. Since the value of \(\sqrt{9} = 3\) is not specified, let's proceed with the general integral.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$I = \int_0^1 9x^{2x} dx$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We find it very useful to introduce a new variable \(f(x) = 2xf'(x)\). Then, substituting this into the integral, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\int f(x) \cdot 9x^{2x} dx$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m From the equation f'=8xf' + 9, we get the new differential \(f'(x) = \frac{1}{8x} (4x + 9)'\). Thus, substituting this into the integral, we obtain:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\int_{0}^{1} 9x^{2x} dx = \int_{0}^{1} 9(1 + \frac{9}{8x})^2 x dx$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m But since \(1 + \frac{9}{8x} > x\), we can simplify it further:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\int_{0}^{1} 9(1 + \frac{9}{8x})^2 x dx = \int_{0}^{1} 9(x + \frac{9}{4})^2 x dx$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Applying integration by parts (or simplifying in two steps), we find:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$I = \left[ x + \frac{9}{4} \times \frac{9}{4} (x^2 + \frac{9}{4}x + \frac{3}{4}) \right]_{0}^{1}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Evaluating from 0 to 1 gives:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$I = \left[ x + \frac{81}{16}(x + \frac{9}{4}x + \frac{3}{4}) \right]_{0}^{1}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m This gives:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$I = \left[1 + \frac{81}{16}(\frac{40}{4} + \frac{3}{4} + \frac{3}{4})\right] - \left[0 + \frac{81}{16}(0)\right]$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Simplifying:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$I = \boxed{\frac{27}{16}}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m AGMAcloud<|endoftext|>
