[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To solve $6 \div 0.\overline{6}$, we first need to convert the repeating decimal $0.\overline{6}$ into a fraction. There are two possible ways to do this:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1) Let $x = 0.\overline{6}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Then $10x = 6.\overline{6}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Subtracting these two equations, we get $9x = 6$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Dividing both sides by 9, we get $x = \dfrac{2}{3}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m By dividing both sides of this equation with $0.\overline{6}$, we get $\dfrac{2}{3} \div 0.\overline{6} = \dfrac{2}{3} \div \dfrac{6}{9} = \dfrac{2 \times 9}{3 \times 6} = \dfrac{18}{18} = 1$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, $6 \div 0.\overline{6} = 1$.
