[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To express \((5 - 4i) - 2(3 + 6i)\) as a complex number, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. Distribute the 2 to each term inside the parentheses:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    (5 - 4i) - 2(3 + 6i) = 5 - 4i - 2 \cdot 3 - 2 \cdot 6i
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Simplify the multiplication:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    5 - 4i - 2 \cdot 3 - 2 \cdot 6i = 5 - 4i - 6 - 12i
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. Combine like terms, which are the real parts and the imaginary parts separately:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    (5 - 6) + (-4i - 12i) = -1 - 16i
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, the complex number is expressed as $\boxed{-1 - 16i}$.<|endoftext|>
