[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To convert $199_{10}$ to base 2, we need to repeatedly divide the number by 2 and record the remainders.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1 Start division: \( 199 \div 2 = 99 \) (with remainder 1) 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2 Continue multiplying 199 by 10 and dividing by 2: 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 199 \times 10 = 1990 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1990 \div 2 = 995 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \text{With remainder } 0
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m After division:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 995 \text{ with remainder } 0 = 199
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So $199 \div 2$ is the equivalent of $995$ divided by $2$. The remainder of the division will be the same as the remainder when splitting the base 10 number into two equals. Therefore, the value of base 2 is: $00000111101_2$.
