[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We're given the point of intersection of the parameterized line, \ not-exterior c, \ with $y = -25$. To find the function $f(t)$, we note that the point of intersection can be on the line $y=-25$, but also on the curve $y = 15t - 7$. In other words, we have the equation \ Given that the points of intersection are: \left(0,\frac{3}{2}\cdot0 - 25\right) and \left(\frac{3}{2}\cdot 6 - 25,\frac{15}{2}\cdot6 - 7\right) \ Notice that the coordinates of the first point are \ (0,\frac{3}{2}\cdot0 - 25\), which means that the point of intersection is $(-6.5, -25). $ \ asy=\frac{3}{2} -15t + 7$ \put(-6.5,-25){$-\dfrac{13}{4}$} \put(-6.5,-25){$+\dfrac{3}{4}$} $\therefore$f(t)=-\dfrac{3}{2}+t+15t-7 \put(-6.5, -25){$-\dfrac{3}{2}$} \put(-6.5 +\frac{3}{4}\frac{13}{4}$) \therefore$f(t)=\dfrac{3}{4}-\dfrac{3}{2}+15t$ $\because$slope $=0\therefore-\dfrac{3}{2} = 0 \therefore \dfrac{3}{4} - \dfrac{3}{2} = 0$
