[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the number of distinct arrangements of the letters in the word "basic", we first need to determine the number of distinct arrangements of the letters. This can be done by using the formula for permutations of a multiset:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\frac{n!}{n_1! \cdot n_2! \cdot \ldots \cdot n_k!}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m where n is the total number of distinct letters, and n1, n2, ..., nk are the counts of each distinct letter in the multiset.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m For the word "basic", there are 5 letters with counts of 1, 2, 3, 2, 5. So, we calculate:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\frac{5!}{1! \cdot 2! \cdot 3! \cdot 2! \cdot 5!}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m This is equivalent to:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\frac{120}{1 \cdot 2 \cdot 6 \cdot 2 \cdot 120}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Hence, there are **240** distinct arrangements of the letters in the word "basic".<|endoftext|>
