[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ \mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ -7 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}, \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ \mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{c} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 7 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}, \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ \mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -7 \\ 18 \end{pmatrix}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m First, let's express \(\mathbf{c} \times (3 \mathbf{a} - 2 \mathbf{b})\) in vector notation.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \mathbf{c} \times (3 \mathbf{a} - 2 \mathbf{b}) = 3 (\mathbf{c} \times \mathbf{a}) - 2 (\mathbf{c} \times \mathbf{b})
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let's find the cross product of 3 direction vectors (e.g., \(\mathbf{c} \times \mathbf{a}\), \(\mathbf{c} \times \mathbf{b}\)).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We notice that:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ (3 \mathbf{a} - 2 \mathbf{b}) = 3 (\mathbf{a} + (- \mathbf{a})) - 2 (\mathbf{b} + (- \mathbf{a})) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Here:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
