[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let \(a = x\). We have the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[2a^3 + 13a^2 - 23a + 8 = 0.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We can try to find integer roots by checking possible factors of the coefficient \(2\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m First, we find the factors of 2:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \(1 \times 2 = 2\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \(2 \times 1 = 2\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The set of integer roots is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[\pm 1, \pm 2.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now we can test each root to see if it satisfies the equation.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. If \(a = 1\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[2(1)^3 + 13(1)^2 - 23(1) + 8 = 2 + 13 - 23 + 8 = 2.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m This is not zero, so \(a = 1\) is not a root.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. If \(a = 2\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[2(2)^3 + 13(2)^2 - 23(2) + 8 = 16 + 52 - 46 + 8 = 20.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m This is not zero, so \(a = 2\) is not a root.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. If \(a = -1\):
