[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m For the nonzero numbers $a$, $b$, and $c$, define $$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \text{{J}}(a,b,c) = \frac{a}{b} + \frac{b}{c} + \frac{c}{a}.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$Find $\text{{J}}(2,12, 9)$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We want to find the value of the expression J(2,12,9).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To do this, we will substitute the given values into the expression and simplify:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m J(2,12,9) &= \frac{2}{12} + \frac{12}{9} + \frac{9}{2} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= \frac{1}{6} + \frac{4}{3} + \frac{9}{2} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= \frac{1 + 36 + 27}{6} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= \frac{74}{6} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= \boxed{\frac{37}{3}}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, the value of the expression J(2,12,9) is $\boxed{\frac{37}{3}}$.
