[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - For 0 sides, there are 1 diagonal.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - For 1 side, there is 1 diagonal.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - For 2 sides, there are 2 diagonals.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - For 3 sides, there are 3 diagonals.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - For 4 sides, there are 4 diagonals.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - For 5 sides, there are 5 diagonals.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, the fifth polygon in the sequence is a pentagon (Fig. 2), which has a total of 5 diagonals.<|endoftext|>
