[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m A $180^\circ$ rotation around the origin in the counter-clockwise direction is applied to $-6 - 3i.$  What is the resulting complex number?
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the resulting complex number after the rotation, we can use Euler's formula, which states that: 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$z=re^{i\theta}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m In this case, we are changing the coordinate system from ECG to ZOP, so we will have $r=r$ and $\theta=\pi/2$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, we have
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[z=re^{i\pi/2}=-6-i\left(0+\sqrt{3}\right)=(0-\sqrt{3})-i6.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Putting it all together, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[\boxed{-0-6i}.\]
