[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m What is the radical conjugate of $2\sqrt{7} - 1$?
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the radical conjugate of $2\sqrt{7} - 1$, we need to take the conjugate of the expression. The radical conjugate is the opposite of all terms within the radical, except the term that has a square root (in this case, $\sqrt{7}$), which remains the same. 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, the radical conjugate of $2\sqrt{7} - 1$ would be:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $2\sqrt{7} + 1$. 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m This is because:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ a + b \sqrt{2} + c \sqrt{3} = a + b (\sqrt{2}+ (-1) \sqrt{3}) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m In this case, the term $\sqrt{7}$, while included, is not changing the radical. We subtract the conjugate of $\sqrt{7}$ it is conjugate to to restore the original expression:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So,
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ 2\sqrt{7} - 1 = 2\sqrt{7} - (\sqrt{7} + 1 \sqrt{7}) \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ 2\sqrt{7} - 1 = 2\sqrt{7} - \sqrt{7} - \sqrt{7} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ 2\sqrt{7} - 1 = 1\sqrt{7} - \sqrt{7} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So,
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ \boxed{1\sqrt{7} - \sqrt{7}} \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m -2\sqrt7-1
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m [Is Boxed Matched]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m True
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
