[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 1: Write a function to check for perfect squares. This function will check if a number is a perfect square. According to mathematical theory, a perfect square is an integer that is the square of an integer (i.e., it can be expressed as \( n^2 \) where \( n \) is an integer). We can use the mathematical property that a number \( a \) is a perfect square if it is the square of an integer. 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 2: Consider this function and count the number of perfect squares between 50 and 250.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
