[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m It seems there was an issue with how the solution was accessed. Instead of solving for \(y\) directly, we can use the fact that the distance from the center \((-1, 2)\) to any point \(P\) on the circle is 18. Since the line segment from the center to any point \(P\) will divide the circle into two parts of equal length, it means that the distance from the center to one section and from the center to the other section together must sum to 18.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let's redefine the variables and set up the equations correctly:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
