[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m This can be rewritten as:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $k - 2 = 2[\log_{10}(k - 2)(k - 1) + 1]$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m or:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $k - 2 = 2 \log_{10}(k - 2)(k - 1)$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now we can use the logarithm power rule, $\log_a(x^y) = y \log_a(x)$, to isolate $\log_{10}(k - 2)(k - 1)$:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $k - 2 = 2[(\log_{10}(k - 1)/0.0301) + 1]$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Simplify the logarithmic expression:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
