[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m In the diagram, $K$, $O$ and $M$ are the centers of the three semi-circles. Also, $OC = 32$ and $CB = 36$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m [asy]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m pair A, K, O, C, M, B, X, Y, Z;
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m O=(0,0);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m C=(32,0);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m M=(50,0);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m B=(68,0);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m A=(-68,0);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m K=(A+C)/2;
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m X=(0,68);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Y=(-18,50);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Z=(50,18);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m path nom, bigc, middlec, smallc;
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m nom=A--B--(100,100)--(-100,100)--cycle;
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m bigc=A..X..B--cycle;
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m middlec=A..Y..C--cycle;
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m smallc=C..Z..B--cycle;
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m fill(bigc, gray(.5));
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m fill(middlec, white);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m fill(smallc, white);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m draw(smallc);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m draw(middlec);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m draw(bigc);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m draw(A--B);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m label("A", A, S);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m label("K", K, S);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m label("O", O, S);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m label("M", M, S);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m label("C", C, S);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m label("B", B, S);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m dot(K);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m dot(O);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m dot(M);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m [/asy]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m What is the area of the semi-circle with center $K$?
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the area of the semi-circle with center \(K\), we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. Calculate the radius of the semi-circle.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Find the area of the full circle.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. Use the fact that the area of a semi-circle is half of the area of the full circle to find the area of the semi-circle with center \(K\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ### Step 1: Calculate the radius of the semi-circle
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Given that \(K\) is the center of the semi-circle and \(OC = 32\), the radius \(r\) of the semi-circle can be found using the Pythagorean theorem in the right triangle \(OCB\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ r = \sqrt{CB^2 - OX^2} = \sqrt{36^2 - OX^2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Since \(O\) is the center of the semicircle, the line from \(O\) perpendicular to \(CB\) bisects \(OC\) and \(CB\). Therefore, \(OX = OX\) because \(O\) is the midpoint of \(OC\). Given \(OC = 32\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ OX = \frac{32}{2} = 16 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So,
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ r = \sqrt{36^2 - 16^2} = \sqrt{1296 - 256} = \sqrt{1040} = 4\sqrt{65} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The diameter of the semi-circle, which is the length of \(AB\), is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ AB = 2 \times 16 = 32 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The radius is half of this, so the full circle radius is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ R = \frac{32}{2} = 16 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ### Step 2: Find the area of the full circle
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The area of a semicircle is half the area of a full circle. The area of a full circle with radius \(R\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ \text{Area of the full circle} = \pi R^2 = \pi \times 16^2 = 256\pi \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ### Step 3: Use the fact that the area of a semi-circle is half of the area of the full circle
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The area of the semi-circle with center \(K\) is half of the area of the full circle:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ \text{Area of the semi-circle with center } K = \frac{\pi R^2}{2} = \frac{\pi (16^2)}{2} = \frac{256\pi}{2} = 128\pi \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, the area of the semi-circle with center \(K\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \(\boxed{128\pi}\)<|endoftext|>
