[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the area of the shaded region, we need to calculate the area of the entire square and then subtract the area of the two regions that were removed.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ### Step 1: Calculate the Area of the Square
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The square has a side length of 8 cm. To find the area, we use the formula for the area of a square:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ \text{area} = \text{side}^2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ \text{area} = 8^2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let's compute this using Python.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m # Define the side length of the square
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m side_length = 8
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m # Calculate the area of the square
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m area = side_length ** 2
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m print(area)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ```
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ```output
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 64
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ```
