[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Since the equation of a circle is $x^2+12y+57=-y^2-10x$,
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m if we rewrite $x^2+10x+y^2+12y=57$ in the form of $$(x+5)^2+(y+6)^2=57+25$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m hence, the center of the circle is $(-5,-6)$, and the radius is $r=\sqrt{{57+25}}=7$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, $a+b+r=-5+(-6)+7=\boxed{-4}$.
