[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Sure, I can help with that. Let's solve the equation step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[\begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \frac{\sin^2 3A}{\sin^2 A} - \frac{\cos^2 3A}{\cos^2 A} &= 2,
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[\cos^2 3A (\sin^2 A - \cos^2 A) + \sin^2 3A \sin^2 A - \sin^2 3A \cos^2 A = 2,\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[\cos^2 3A (\sin^2 A - \cos^2 A) + \sin^4 A - \sin^2 3A \cos^2 A = 2,\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[2 \cos^2 3A \sin^2 A - 2 \cos^2 A \sin^2 A + \sin^4 A - \sin^2 3A \cos^2 A = 2,\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[2 \cos^2 3A \sin^2 A - 2 \cos^2 A \sin^2 A + \sin^4 A = 3 \cos^2 3A \sin^2 A,\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[\sin^2 A (4 \cos^2 3A - 2 \cos^2 A + 1) = 3 \cos^2 3A \sin^2 A.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Since we are considering \( \cos 2A \), it is easier to make the denominator the same. Writing each term with the same denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[\begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2 \cos^2 3A \sin^2 A - 2 \cos^2 A \sin^2 A + \sin^4 A &= 3 \cos^2 3A \sin^2 A, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4 \cos^4 3A - 2 \cos^2 3A + 1 &= 3 \cos^2 3A \sin^2 A, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4 \cos^4 3A (1 - \sin^2 A) - 2 \cos^2 3A + 1 - 3 \cos^2 3A \sin^2 A &= 0.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m As it appears that \( \cos^2 3A \sin^2 A \) is unaffected by adding and subtracting a term with algebraic difference of squares:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[4 \cos^4 3A - 2 \cos^2 3A + 1 - 3 \cos^2 3A \sin^2 A = 0.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m After substituting \( \cos^2 3A = \csc^2 3A \) and \( \cos^2 3A \sin^2 A = \csc^2 3A \sin 3A \), the equation is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[\csc^2 3A (\csc^4 A - \csc^2 A + 1 - 1) = 0,\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m which is clear because the left side is just \( 0 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Since it equals the right side, the only x that worked is the solutions where \( \csc^2 3A \sin^2 A = 0 \), i.e., 0, causing \( \sin 3A = 0 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m This assumption yields \( \sin 3A = 0 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So \\(\sin 3A = 0 \Rightarrow 3A = 45^\circ\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \boxed{\frac{1}{2}}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
