[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let $\theta$ be an angle such that $\tan \theta = 2.$  Simplify
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[\frac{e^{2i \theta} - 1}{e^{2i \theta} + 1}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let $\theta = \arctan\left(\frac{2}{1}\right) = \arctan(2)$ be the argument of the reciprocal of $2,$ $\theta = \frac{\pi}{\arre{\tan(2)}}.$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The Euler's formula gives
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[e^{2i\theta}-1=e^{2i\tan^{-1(2)}},\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m and therefore
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \frac{e^{2i\theta}-1}{e^{2i\theta}+1}&=\frac{e^{2i\tan^{-1(2)}}}{e^{2i\tan^{-1(2)}}+1}\\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= \cos(2\theta)+\sin(2\theta)\\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m & = \cos\left(2 \arctan(\frac{2}{1})+\pi\right) +\sin\left(2 \arctan(\frac{2}{1})+\pi\right)\\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m & =\frac{2}{\sqrt{5}}+\frac{3}{\sqrt{5}}.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The answer is: \frac{5+2\sqrt{5}}{5}<|endoftext|>
