[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let us assume that the answer is 169.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Then,
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $169x^3 - 31x^2 - 34x - 7 = (x^2 + 5x + 1)(169x - 100)$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Rewriting the expression inside the bracket,
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $169x - 100 = 11x(15 - x)$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So it remains as
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $11x(15x - 100)$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now as an integer divides by a factor times a non-zero integer. Thus,
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $11x(15x - 100)$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Is virtually divisible by $1$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Thus it doesn't give zero remainder.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Finally, taking $x = 1$.
