[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now we need to multiply these exponents together:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ 10^{\frac{1}{2}} \cdot 10^{\frac{3}{10}} \cdot 10^{\frac{2}{5}} \cdot 10^{1} \cdot 10^{\frac{9}{10}} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Using the rule \(a^m \cdot a^n = a^{m+n}\), we can combine the exponents:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ 10^{\left(\frac{1}{2} + \frac{3}{10} + \frac{2}{5} + 1 + \frac{9}{10}\right)} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Next, we simplify the sum of the exponents:
