[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the minimum value of $a^2 + 2b^2 + c^2$ given that $a + b + c = 1,$ we can apply AM-GM inequality to the expression. According to the AM-GM inequality, for any non-negative numbers $x,$ $y,$ $z,$ we have $\frac{x + y + z}{3} \geqslant \sqrt[3]{xyz}.$ In this case, we have $a,$ $b,$ $c$ as the terms $x$ $y$ $z.$ Applying $\displaystyle\frac{1}{3} \geqslant \sqrt[3]{3}$ for equality, we get
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m a + b + c &= 1 &\implies &a + b + c \geqslant c \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &\implies & a + b \geqslant 1 - c
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m And the minimum value of $a^2 + 2b^2 + c^2$ becomes 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[\boxed{a^2 + 2b^2 + c^2 = a^2 + 2(b + c - c)^2 \geqslant a^2 + 2(1 - c)^2 = 2a^2 - 4a + 2b^2 + c^2 + 2c^2 - 2c^2 = 2a^2 - 4a + 2a^2 - 2c^2 + 4ac + 2bc}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Since $a,$ $b,$ $c$ are positive real numbers,
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m we have $a^2 \geqslant a \geqslant \displaystyle\frac{a^2}{4a} \geqslant \displaystyle\frac{a^2}{4} \geqslant a,$ similarly $2b^2 \geqslant b,$ and $c^2 \geqslant c$ for positive $a,$ $b,$ $c.$ Therefore, the minimum value of $a^2 + 2b^2 + c^2$ is $\boxed{2(a^2 + 2b^2 + c^2)}.$
