[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4. **Perform the calculations**:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    C' = (0, 3)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, the coordinates of the image of point \(C\) after a 90-degree counterclockwise rotation about \(B\) are \(\boxed{(0, 3)}\).<|endoftext|>
