[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To complete the expression, we'll first remove the parentheses, and then combine like terms. Here's the step-by-step solution:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. Start with the given expression:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[(9x^5 + 25x^3 - 4) - (x^5 - 3x^3 - 4).\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Distribute the negative sign through the second set of parentheses:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[9x^5 + 25x^3 - 4 - x^5 + 3x^3 + 4.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. Combine like terms:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[9x^5 - x^5 + 25x^3 + 3x^3 - 4 - 4.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4. Simplify the coefficients and like terms:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \#[9x^5 - x^5] + [25x^3 + 3x^3] - 8 = 8x^5 + 28x^3 - 8.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, the completely factored expression is \[8x^5 + 28x^3 - 8.\]
