[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m How many vertical asymptotes does the graph of
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[y = \frac{(x + 3)^5 (x + 2)^8 (x + 1)^4 (x - 7)^2}{(x + 3)^{11} (x + 2)^6 (x + 1)^4 x^2}\]have?
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the vertical asymptotes of the given rational function,
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[y = \frac{(x + 3)^5 (x + 2)^8 (x + 1)^4 (x - 7)^2}{(x + 3)^{11} (x + 2)^6 (x + 1)^4 (x^2)^2},\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m we need to find the values of \(x\) that make the denominator zero, as these will be special undefined points of the function.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Given the denominator,
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m (x + 3)^{11} (x + 2)^6 (x + 1)^4 (x^2)^2 &= (x + 3)^{11} (x + 2)^6 (x + 1)^4 x^2\cdot x^2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= (x + 3)^{11} (x + 2)^6 (x + 1)^4 x^4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= (x + 3)^{11} (x + 2)^6 (x + 1)^4 x^4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= (x + 3)^{11} (x + 2)^6 (x + 1)^4 x^2.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m This makes the denominator zero when either factor is zero. So,
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[x + 3 = 0, \quad x + 2 = 0, \quad x + 1 = 0.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Solving these equations,
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m x + 3 &= 0 \implies x = -3, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m x + 2 &= 0 \implies x = -2, \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m x + 1 &= 0 \implies x = -1.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Thus, the vertical asymptotes occur at \(x = -3\), \(x = -2\), and \(x = -1\). Therefore, there are \(\boxed{3}\) vertical asymptotes on the graph.<|endoftext|>
