[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let $A = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & -1 \\ 7 & 2 \end{pmatrix}.$ Then $A^{2} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & -1 \\ 7 & 2 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix}2 & -1 \\ 7 & 2 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 19 & 10 \\ 19 & 10 \end{pmatrix}.$ Therefore,the determinant of $A$ is $19 \cdot 10 - 10 \cdot 19 = -6,$ and we can read off the following formulas for the values of $A^{n-1}$ for positive integers $n:$$A^{1} = A - 6I.$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m It follows that $A^{2019} = (-6)^{1009} (2 \cdot 7 - (-1) \cdot 7) = 4 \cdot (-1).$<|endoftext|>
