[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the coordinates of the other endpoint, we need to understand the midpoint of all points on the line segment. The midpoint $$(x_c, y_c)$$ of a line segment connecting two points$$(x_1, y_1)$$ and$$(x_2, y_2)$$ can be found using the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$x_c = \frac{x_1 + x_2}{2} \quad \text{and} \quad y_c = \frac{y_1 + y_2}{2}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Given the endpoints of the segment: $$(6, 8)$$ and $$(1, 1)$$, let’s denote:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - $$(x_1, y_1)$$ is the first point of the line (coordinates given):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m   $$x_1 = 6, \quad y_1 = 8$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - $$(x_2, y_2)$$ is the second point of the line ($$x_2 = 1$$, denote this as point$$A\quad ).$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m First, calculate the x-coordinate of midpoint:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$x_c = \frac{x_1 + x_2}{2} = \frac{6 + 1}{2} = \frac{7}{2}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Then, calculate the y-coordinate of midpoint:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$y_c = \frac{y_1 + y_2}{2} = \frac{8 + 1}{2} = \frac{9}{2}$$   
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, using midpoint coordinates, we can calculate the coordinates of the other endpoint$$B\quad $$(coordinates given):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$B_x = x_c$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$B_y = y_c$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Setting $$x_b = 1$$ using midpoint x-coordinate and plug it into the equation for \(B_y\) to get the point $$B\quad $$(coordinates given) : 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$1 = \frac{9/2}{1} = \frac{1}{\frac{1}{2}}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So the coordinates with point B are:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\boxed{(1, 1)}$$
