[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The coefficient of $b^{m+1}$ in the above equation must give a units digit of $7$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let us consider the case when $m$ is a multiple of $3$ and suppose $m=3k$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m mn&=3kb
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Also, the sum of adjacent coefficients must be similar to the value of the coefficients of $b^{m+1}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Taking mod $10$,
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
