[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To solve this, first note that 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$10^{2000}+10^{2002} = 2\times 10^{2000}$$ and 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$10^{2001}+10^{2001} = 2\times 10^{2001}\text{.}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, our ratio becomes 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\frac{2\times 10^{2000}}{2\times 10^{2001}} = \frac{10^{2000}}{10^{2001}}\text{.}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\frac{10^{2000}}{10^{2001}} = 10^{-1}\text{.}$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We can see that 10-1 is 9, which is the closest whole number to $\boxed{{9}}$.
