[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    45 \left(\frac{3}{5}\right) \left(\frac{7}{9}\right)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    First, multiply \(\frac{3}{5}\) and \(\frac{7}{9}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \frac{3}{5} \times \frac{7}{9} = \frac{3 \times 7}{5 \times 9} = \frac{21}{45}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    Simplify \(\frac{21}{45}\) by finding the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 21 and 45, which is 3:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \frac{21}{45} = \frac{21 \div 3}{45 \div 3} = \frac{7}{15}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    Now, multiply \(\frac{7}{15}\) by \(\frac{3}{5}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \frac{7}{15} \times \frac{3}{5} = \frac{7 \times 3}{15 \times 5} = \frac{21}{75}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    Simplify \(\frac{21}{75}\) by finding the GCD of 21 and 75, which is 3:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \frac{21}{75} = \frac{21 \div 3}{75 \div 3} = \frac{7}{25}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4. **Combine the simplified numerator and denominator:**
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \frac{10}{\frac{7}{25}}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    Dividing by a fraction is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \frac{10}{\frac{7}{25}} = 10 \times \frac{25}{7} = \frac{10 \times 25}{7} = \frac{250}{7}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, the value of \(\frac{5x+9y}{45xy}\) when \(x = \frac{3}{5}\) and \(y = \frac{7}{9}\) is \(\boxed{\frac{250}{7}}\).<|endoftext|>
