[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To simplify the given expression \(\frac{1 + \sin x - \cos x}{1 + \sin x + \cos x}\), we can use a trigonometric identity to combine the terms on the numerator and the denominator.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The identity we will use is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \sin x + \cos x = \sqrt{2} \sin\left(x + \frac{\pi}{4}\right),
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m where \(\sin\left(x + \frac{\pi}{4}\right) = \frac{\sin x + \cos x}{2}\), hence \(\sin x + \cos x = \sqrt{2} \sin\left(x + \frac{\pi}{4}\right)\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \frac{1 + \sin x - \cos x}{1 + \sin x + \cos x} = \frac{1 + \sqrt{2} \sin\left(x + \frac{\pi}{4}\right) - \cos x}{1 + \sqrt{2} \sin\left(x + \frac{\pi}{4}\right) + \cos x}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, factor \(1 + \sqrt{2} \sin\left(x + \frac{\pi}{4}\right)\) out of the two fractions on the left-hand side:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1 + \sin x - \cos x = (\sqrt{2} \sin\left(x + \frac{\pi}{4}\right)) \times \text{coefficient}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1 + \sin x + \cos x = \text{coefficient} \times (\sqrt{2}),
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m where the \(\text{coefficient}\) means the product of the terms under the square root without the \(\sqrt{2}\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \text{coefficient} = (\sqrt{2} \times \sin\left(x + \frac{\pi}{4}\right)) = \sqrt{2} \sin\left(x + \frac{\pi}{4}\right).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Thus, we have:
