[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m What is the units digit of the product of the first three positive composite numbers?
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To determine the units digit of the product of the first three positive composite numbers, we need to first identify those numbers.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. The first three positive composite numbers are:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - 4 (since \(4 = 2 \times 2\))
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - 6 (since \(6 = 2 \times 3\))
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - 8 (since \(8 = 2 \times 4\))
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Now, find the units digit of each of these numbers:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - \(4\) has a units digit of \(4\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - \(6\) has a units digit of \(6\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - \(8\) has a units digit of \(8\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. Identify the common units digit across all three numbers:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - The unit digit of \(4\) is \(4\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - The unit digit of \(6\) is \(6\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - The unit digit of \(8\) is \(8\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4. The units digit of their multiplication would be:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - \(4 \times 6 \times 8\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 5. Calculate the multiplication of the units digits:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    4 \times 6 = 24 \quad \text{(units digit is } 4\text{)}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    4 \times 8 = 32 \quad \text{(units digit is } 2\text{)}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    24 \times 2 = 48 \quad \text{(units digit is } 8\text{)}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 6. Therefore, the units digit of \(4 + 6 + 8\) is \(8\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Conclusion:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \boxed{8}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
