[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m On a protractor, ray $BA$ goes through the 85-degree mark and ray $BC$ goes through the 30-degree mark. What is the measure, in degrees, of angle $ABC$?
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m [asy]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m draw((0,0)--(2,0)..(1,1)..(0,0)..cycle,linewidth(2));
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m draw((1,0)--1.4dir(30)+(1,0),Arrow);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m draw((1,0)--1.3dir(85)+(1,0),Arrow);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m dot(1.1dir(85)+(1,0));
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m dot(1.2dir(30)+(1,0));
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m label("A",1.1dir(85)+(1,0),NW);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m label("B",(1,0),S);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m label("C",1.2dir(30)+(1,0),SE);
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m label("85",.9dir(85)+(1,0));
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m label("30",.9dir(30)+(1,0));
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m [/asy]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the measure of angle \( \angle ABC \), we can use the properties of angles formed by a transversal crossing two parallel lines.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. Ray \( BA \) goes through the 85-degree mark.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Ray \( BC \) goes through the 30-degree mark.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Since \( BA \) is parallel to \( BC \), we can use the fact that if two parallel lines are cut by a transversal, the measure of angle \( \angle ABC \) is equal to the sum of the exterior angles formed by \( BA \) and \( BC \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The measure of the exterior angle to \( BA \) is \( 180^\circ - 85^\circ = 95^\circ \) because it is an angle formed by a transversal crossing two parallel lines.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The measure of the exterior angle to \( BC \) is \( 180^\circ - 30^\circ = 150^\circ \) because it is an angle formed by a transversal crossing two parallel lines.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, the measure of \( \angle ABC \) is \( 95^\circ + 150^\circ = 245^\circ \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Here is the more formal calculation using Protractor System:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. Assign a coordinate plane to \( BA \) and \( BC \), starting at \( A \) with \( x = 0 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Place point \( B \) on the positive x-axis.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. Draw a line from \( A \) to \( B \) and from \( B \) to \( C \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4. Enumerate each side meeting:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - Corresponding angles: \( \angle BAC \), \( \angle BCA \), and \( \angle ACB \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - Interior angles: \( \angle BAC \), \( \angle BCA \), and \( \angle ACB \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Measure the exterior sum of angles due to transversal:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - Exterior angle to \( BA \): \( 95^\circ \)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - Exterior angle to \( BC \): \( 150^\circ \)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Sum of interior angles:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ \angle BAC + \angle BCA + \angle ACB = 95^\circ + 150^\circ = 245^\circ \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, the measure of \( \angle ABC \) is \( \boxed{245} \).<|endoftext|>
