[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Sure, let's find the sum of the positive divisors of 18. 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. Calculate all the positive divisors of 18:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - Start from 1 and continue up to 18 (inclusive). 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - We need to check each number, since 1 is not a divisor of anything.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Go through each of these numbers.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - If a number is greater than 1, it is a divisor.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - And make sure we don't draw the number again.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let's do this step-by-step:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - 1 is a proper divisor and will only be added once.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - 2 divides 18 without a remainder: \( 18 \div 2 = 9 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      - Snapshot: 2, 9
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - 3 divides 18 without a remainder: \( 18 \div 3 = 6 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      - Snapshot: 3, 6
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - 6 divides 18 without a remainder: \( 18 \div 6 = 3 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      - Snapshot: 6, 3
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - 9 divides 18 without a remainder: \( 18 \div 9 = 2 \)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m      - Snapshot: 9, 2
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - And so on until 18.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m   
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - Accumulator sums to our perpetuation of 9, 3, 2.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The sum of divisors of 18 comprises : 1 + 2 + 3 + 6 + 9 + 18 = 37.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m boxed{37}<|endoftext|>
