[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let $m$ be the number of positive divisors of $n$. Then the equation we want to solve is
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{equation*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m     \frac{1}{2}(m-1)=(n\mid 729)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{equation*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $m$'s prime factorization should be 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m     729=3^{6} &\Rightarrow \quad m=6+1=7 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m     729=3^{3}.\cdot3^{3} &\Rightarrow \quad m=3+1=4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $\left|\overline{m,n}\right|\leq 2$ so $4<m \leq 7$. Then $\boxed{n = \boxed{4192}}$.ynecgraphicsysystem<|endoftext|>
