[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m When $555_{10}$ is expressed in this base, it has 4 digits, in the form ABAB, where A and B are two different digits.  What base is it?
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Yes, wait for a moment for us to go through the logic.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m "It $(A + B) \times B = A \times B + B \times B" applied to our given expression. In the same manner that Identities for $\A\times 1$ and $\1\times \B$ are valid formulas for $A$ and $B$ each assuming $X$ has a 7 digit expression, then based on your other equation, we could solve for A & B.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m First, at this point we represent it as the following values:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $\A\,=\,\overline {555_{10}} \,\,= \,1131$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $\Rightarrow A \equiv 1 \,\,\,; \,\,\,B \:= \,1 \,\,\, ( 1131 \text{ digit})$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Reindex $Change!2$ of each A and B to A+X and X+Y as follows in matrix style.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \dfrac112&=X+Y&[End]=0001\\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \dfrac12&=1+X& [End]=001\\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \frac1{10}&=X&[End]=100\\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \dfrac110&=Y& [End]=\overline{1001011} \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Subsequent calculations starting from above will ultimately yield a result of 688.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
