[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. This means the part that Ben does is $\frac{5}{8}$ of the whole fence.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. To find out how much Ben paints, we need to calculate $\frac{5}{8}$ of 240 square feet:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \text{Part} = \frac{240 \times 5}{8} = \frac{240 \times 5}{8} = \frac{240}{8} = 30
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, Ben paints $\boxed{30}$ square feet.<|endoftext|>
