[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To solve the equation \(\frac{5x}{(x+3)} - \frac3{(x+3)} = \frac1{(x+3)}\), we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. Simplify the left-hand side of the equation. Since both fractions have the same denominator, they can be combined into a single fraction:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \frac{5x}{(x+3)} - \frac{3}{(x+3)} = \frac{5x - 3}{(x+3)}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    So the equation becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \frac{5x - 3}{(x+3)} = \frac1{(x+3)}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Eliminate the denominators by multiplying both sides of the equation by \((x+3)\), which is the least common multiple of the denominators \(x+3\) and \((x+3)\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    5x - 3 = 1
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. Isolate \(x\) by adding 3 to both sides of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    5x = 4
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4. Solve for \(x\) by dividing both sides by 5:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    x = \frac{4}{5}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The solution to the equation is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \boxed{\frac{4}{5}}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
