[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m C: $x_{1}=1$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m D: $x_{2}=-1$ First, we need to note that the roots of the quadratic equation $x^{2} - 1 = 0$ are given by the roots of the equation in the form $x^{2} = 1$. This implies that $x = 1 \text{ or } x = -1$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Next, we are given that one of the roots is $x = 2$. We will substitute this value into the equation $x^{2} = 1$ to find the other root:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2^{2} &= 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 5 &= 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, we find the equation $x^{2} - 1$ by replacing $x$ with $5$:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 5^{2} - 1 &= 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 25 - 1 & = 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 24 &= 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Hence, the other root is $x = 24 - 1 = 23$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, the correct answer is $(D)x_{2}=-1.$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Thus, the final result is: $\boxed{D}$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To summarize, the equation $x^{2} = 1$ and substituting $x = 2$ will yield $x^{2} - 1 = 0$, from which $x = -1$ can be derived. The other root of the equation is $23$. The answer will be encapsulated in the final boxed response.
