[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m A number $x$ factors as $107\cdot109^5$, and $107$ and $109$ are primes. What is the exponent of $109$ in the prime factorization of $x^{11}$?
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $107 = 1727$. $109^5 = 5385429$. From highest to lowest prime factors, $109$ is a smaller factor. $107$ and $109$ are prime numbers, so $x = 109^5\cdot1727^5 = 10^5\cdot7\cdot3^1\cdot5\cdot11^5\cdot13^5$. So, the exponent of $109$ in the prime factorization of $x^{11}$ is $1 + 5 = 6$.<|endoftext|>
