[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To solve for the value of \( p(q(2)) \) where \( p(x) = 2 - x^2 \) and \( q(x) = \frac{6}{x} \), we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. Calculate \( q(2) \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Use the result from step 1 to compute \( p(q(2)) \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let's proceed step-by-step.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ### Step 1: Calculate \( q(2) \)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Given \( q(x) = \frac{6}{x} \), we substitute \( x = 2 \):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m q(2) = \frac{6}{2} = 3
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ### Step 2: Compute \( p(q(2)) \)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We know \( p(x) = 2 - x^2 \), and since \( q(2) = 3 \), we need to find \( p(q(2)) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m p(q(2)) = p(3)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Substitute \( x = 3 \) into \( p(x) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m p(3) = 2 - 3^2 = 2 - 9 = -7
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Thus, \( p(q(2)) = -7 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ### Conclusion
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The value of \( p(q(2)) \) is \(\boxed{-7}\).
