[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Compute $\tan 150^\circ$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 1: Understand the trigonometric ratio for 150 degrees
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The 150 degrees is in the second quadrant, where the tangent is positive and in the second quadrant, we have the reference angle of 150 - $\pi$ in the first quadrant.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 2: Calculate $150^\circ$ in radians
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Taking the complement of the angle, 150 degrees will be $60^\circ$, and since it's in the second quadrant, we need to convert it into the first quadrant. 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 3: Perform the trigonometric calculation for tangent
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m By using the difference formula in trigonometry, 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \mathit{\tan}^\alpha \gleu -b\\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= \sep( \sep \tan \gleu -b \tercentage \sepa)- (\sep(\approx 60^\circ)>=)\\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= \sep (\frac{\tan b-\tan 60^\circ}{1-\tan b \cdot \tan 60^\circ})\\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= \sep (\frac{1-\sqrt{3}}{\frac{1}{\sqrt{3}}}\\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= \sep (\frac{1-\sqrt{3}}{1/\sqrt{3}})\\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &=\text{2}.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, $\tan 60^\circ = 2$. This is the exact solution in a precise mathematical context.
