[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To solve the equation $4x^{1/3}-2 \cdot \frac{x}{x^{2/3}}=7+\sqrt[3]{x}$, we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. Simplify the equation.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Isolate the fractional term to form a quadratic equation.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. Solve the quadratic equation for $x$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let's take a look at the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $4x^{1/3}-2 \cdot \frac{x}{x^{2/3}}=7+\sqrt[3]{x}$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m (Simplifying the terms)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We get:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $4x^{1/3}-2x^{\frac{1}{3}-1}=7+x^{\frac{1}{3}}$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Next, we'll isolate the fractional term using inverse operations.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Integrating both sides to get the form of $\bf{ \large x^{\frac{1}{3}}}$:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m For the left side, use the substitution method:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m substitute $t=x^{\frac{1}{3}}$: 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $\frac{3}{2}t^2-\frac{2}{3}t^{1/3}$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m For the right side, let's assume$\bf x\approx 1$: 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $\bf x = 1=> \bf 4\bf x^{1/3}=> 1 \approx x^{\frac{1}{3}}=> x = 1$ 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m As there are no closed form solutions for $x\iff 1$ or beyond, integration can't be applied directly. So we have to use another method.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Consider a plug flow as the chemical-water interaction, namely  which is suitable for in water solubility as well as gas absorption solubility case.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Thus we can form the partial volume (passive vapor mass flux) from the gas point&lightning<=>ice bar
