[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[\mathbf{a} = k (1, 1 + \sin \theta, 1)\]and
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[\mathbf{b} = k (1 + \cos \theta, 1, 1)\]where $k$ is a constant. We'll use the determinant formula to express this determinant:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1 & k(1 + \sin \theta) & k(1) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1 & 1 + \sin \theta & k(1) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1 + k \cos \theta & 1 & k 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Expanding the determinant along the first row:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b} - \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{a} - \mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b} = 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{vmatrix} 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1 & 1 + \sin \theta & 1  \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1 & 1 + \sin \theta & 1  \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1 + k \cos \theta & 1 & k 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m With c = k*(-1**2 c**2* cos c + k **2 c**2* **c**/2)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Thus the determinant:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
