[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We need to find the number of different 3-edge trips from $A$ to $B$. There are three types of trips from $A$ to $B$ that involve each traversal of edges $a$, $b$, and $c$ of the cube. This can be represented by $3!$ (factorial of 3) outcomes, where the first order is not affected by the choice of order in different quantities. The sequences are $a b c b, a b c b a$, and $a b c a b$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m There are three choices for the order in which to traverse the edges. This results in $3!$ possible triples. There are therefore $3\times 3=\boxed{9}$ different 3-edge trips from $A$ to $B$.怠accept your answer! coolant<|endoftext|>
