[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To solve the equation \(\log_5(x-18) = 2\), we need to convert it to its exponential form.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. Recognize that \(\log_5(x-18)\) is the exponent to which 5 must be raised to obtain \(x-18\). Therefore, we can rewrite the equation as:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    5^2 = x - 18
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Simplify the left side of the equation. Since \(5^2 = 25\), the equation becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    25 = x - 18
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. To isolate \(x\), add 18 to both sides of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    25 + 18 = x
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4. Perform the addition:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    43 = x
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Thus, the solution to the equation \(\log_5(x-18)=2\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \boxed{43}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
