[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let $a,$ $b,$ $c$ be the roots of $x^3 + px + q = 0.$  Express
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[\begin{vmatrix} 1 + a & 1 & 1 \\ 1 & 1 + b & 1 \\ 1 & 1 & 1 + c \end{vmatrix}\]in terms of $p$ and $q.$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let's begin by recognizing that the given determinant is a cubic determinant with a specific form. We can use properties of determinants and symmetry to simplify our calculations.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The determinant is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m D = \begin{vmatrix} 1 + a & 1 & 1 \\ 1 & 1 + b & 1 \\ 1 & 1 & 1 + c \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To simplify this, let's recognize that each element of the matrix is influenced by the respective diagonal elements \((a, b, c)\). We can use cofactor expansion along the first row.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m D = 1 \left(\begin{vmatrix} 1 + b & 1 \\ 1 & 1 + c \end{vmatrix}\right) - 1 \left(\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 1 \\ 1 & 1 + c \end{vmatrix}\right) + 1 \left(\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 1 + b \\ 1 & 1 \end{vmatrix}\right)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, we calculate each of these determinants separately.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. \(\begin{vmatrix} 1 + b & 1 \\ 1 & 1 + c \end{vmatrix} = (1 + b)(1 + c) - 1 \cdot 1 = (1 + b)(1 + c) - 1\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. \(\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 1 \\ 1 & 1 + c \end{vmatrix} = 1 \cdot (1 + c) - 1 \cdot 1 = 1 + c - 1 = c\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. \(\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 1 + b \\ 1 & 1 \end{vmatrix} = 1 \cdot 1 - 1 \cdot (1 + b) = 1 - (1 + b) = 1 - 1 - b = -b\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Putting it all together, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m D = 1 \left((1 + b)(1 + c) - 1\right) - 1(c) + 1(-b)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m D = (1 + b)(1 + c) - 1 - c - b
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m D = 1 + c + b + bc - 1 - c - b
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m D = bc
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, the determinant is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \boxed{bc}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
