[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The natural numbers between 6 and 60 that are relatively prime to 15 will be numbers that do not share common factors with 15. One of these numbers is always 1 since 15 is divisible by 1. Then, we exclude 1, so only the numbers 2, 3, 5, and 7 are relatively prime to 15.
