[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let's find the equation of the plane passing through the point \( (0, 7, -7) \) and containing the line given by
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \(\frac{x + 1}{-3} = \frac{y - 3}{2} = \frac{z + 2}{1}.\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m First, identify the direction vector of the line. The line passes through the origin \((0, 0, 0)\) and makes an angle of \(60^\circ\) with both coordinate axes. The direction vector can be represented as \(\mathbf{d} = \langle -3, 2, 1 \rangle\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The normal vector \(\mathbf{n}\) to the plane can be found by taking the dot product of \(\mathbf{d}\) with the direction vector of the line. The equation of the plane in point-normal form is \(A \cdot (x - x_0) + B \cdot (y - y_0) + C \cdot (z - z_0) = 0\), where \((x_0, y_0, z_0)\) is a point on the plane.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Substitute \((x_0, y_0, z_0) = (0, 0, 0)\) into the plane equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[A \cdot (0 - x) + B \cdot (0 - y) + C \cdot (0 - z) = 0.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[-Ax + By - Cz = 0.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, the equation of the plane is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[-3x + 2y - z = 0.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
