[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Given the functions $f(x)=\dfrac{x+5}{3}$ and $g(x)=\dfrac{1}{f^{-1}(x)+1}$, find the value of $g(3)$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the value of \( g(3) \), we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. Determine the value of \( f^{-1}(x) \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Use the value of \( f^{-1}(x) \) to find \( g(x) \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 1: Determine the value of \( f^{-1}(x) \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The function \( f(x) = \dfrac{x+5}{3} \) can be inverted by solving for \( x \) in terms of \( y \):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ y = \dfrac{x+5}{3} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ 3y = x + 5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ x = 3y - 5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, \( f^{-1}(x) = 3x - 5 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 2: Use the value of \( f^{-1}(x) \) to find \( g(x) \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We have \( g(x) = \dfrac{1}{f^{-1}(x) + 1} \). Substituting \( f^{-1}(x) = 3x - 5 \) into this equation, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ g(x) = \dfrac{1}{3x - 5 + 1} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ g(x) = \dfrac{1}{3x - 4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, we need to find \( g(3) \):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ g(3) = \dfrac{1}{3(3) - 4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ g(3) = \dfrac{1}{9 - 4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ g(3) = \dfrac{1}{5} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, the value of \( g(3) \) is \(\boxed{\dfrac{1}{5}}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \dfrac{1}{5}
