[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m For the set of vectors $\left\{ \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}, \begin{pmatrix} k \\ -2 \end{pmatrix} \right\}$ to be linearly independent, each vector must be a linear combination of the other two with coefficients not all-zero.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Knowing that each vector is a linear combination of $\left\{ \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}, \begin{pmatrix} k \\ -2 \end{pmatrix} \right\}$, we can write two equations as follows.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}=a \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}+b \begin{pmatrix} k \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $\begin{pmatrix} k \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}=d \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}+e \begin{pmatrix} k \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The first equation gives $a+kb=dk+e$ for all values of both $b$ and $d$. This equation is satisfied unless $a = 0$ and $d = 0$, which means $k=0$ and $e=0$. Conversely, if $k=0$, the vector becomes $\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}$. 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, the equation $\begin{pmatrix} k \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}$ must be congruent to a scalar multiple of $\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}$. Therefore, $a=0$ and $e=0$, giving us the reduced equation $-2e = (-2)k=(-2)$. Solving these equations gives $k \in \boxed{\mathbb R \setminus \{-1\}}$.
