[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Arnold will water and feed his cactus plants on the same day for the second time until he needs to repeat his previous watering and feeding sequence for at least the next 9 days and also he needs to repeat his feeding sequence for 60 days as per the given problem. Let's calculate the days it will take for the time reversal.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Arnold will water and feed his cactus plant 9 days ago, so we have on the first day of his new sequence:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Jan  = 0 = 1 day back
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Jan 31th is 31 days since the day he was last watering and feeding. 8 days ago:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Jan 32 = 31 days - 30 days = 1 day back
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We continue this until we reach the end of his next watering and feeding week:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Dec 31 = 31 days - 30 days = 1 day back
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Dec 32 = 31 days - 30 days + 1 day = 2 days back
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Dec 33 = 31 days - 30 days + 2 days = 3 days back
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Dec 34 = 31 days - 30 days + 3 days = 4 days back
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Dec 35 = 31 days - 30 days + 4 days = 5 days back, and he will again begin the same watering and feeding sequence for Jan - 3 days.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Dec 36 = 31 days - 30 days + 5 days = 6 days back, and he will begin another watering and feeding sequence for Jan - 6 days.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Dec 37 = 31 days - 30 days + 6 days = 7 days back, and he will begin another watering and feeding sequence for Jan - 7 days.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Dec 38 = 31 days - 30 days + 7 days = 8 days back, and he will begin another watering and feeding sequence for Jan - 8 days.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Dec 39 = 31 days - 30 days + 8 days = 9 days back, and he will begin another watering and feeding sequence for Jan - 9 days.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Dec 40 = 31 days - 30 days + 9 days = 10 days back, and he will begin another watering and feeding sequence for Jan - 10 days.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Dec 41 = 31 days - 30 days + 10 days = 11 days back, and he will begin another watering and feeding sequence for Jan - 11 days.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Dec 42 = 31 days - 30 days + 11 days = 12 days back, and he will begin another watering and feeding sequence for Jan - 12 days, and it is Sunday tomorrow.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
