[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ n \equiv -3736 \pmod{6} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m This means we are looking for an integer \( n \) that, when subtracted by 3736, is divisible by 6. This is equivalent to finding an integer \( n \) such that:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ n + 3736 \equiv 0 \pmod{6} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m This means we need:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ n \equiv -3736 \pmod{6} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To make it simpler, we can find the remainder when 3736 is divided by 6:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ 3736 \div 6 = 622 \text{ remainder } 4 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So,
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ 3736 \equiv 4 \pmod{6} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, to make \(-3736\) leave a remainder of 0 when divided by 6, we can simply subtract this remainder from 3736:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ n \equiv -4 \pmod{6} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Since \(-4\) is equivalent to 2 (since \(-4 + 4 = 0\)), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ n \equiv 2 \pmod{6} \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Finally, we need to find \( n \) within the range \( 0 \leq n \leq 5 \). Therefore, we take:
