[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To calculate the number of different combinations that can be drawn, we use the "permutations with repetition" rule.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The formula for permutations with repetition is: (number of items)^(number of duplicates)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m In this case, the number of items is 50 (total number of balls), and the number of duplicates is 3.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, the number of combinations which can be drawn is: 50^(3) = 50 * 50 * 50 = 125000
