[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let $\mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} -7 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\mathbf{w} = \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}.$  Find the area of the parallelogram with vertices $\mathbf{0},$ $\mathbf{v},$ $\mathbf{w},$ and $\mathbf{v} + \mathbf{w}.$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We must compute the projection of $\mathbf{v}$ on $\mathbf{w},$ which is
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$v\times w=\mathbf{v}\cdot \mathbf{w} \begin{pmatrix} w_2 \\ w_3 \end{pmatrix} = ( -7 )\cdot 5 + ( 1 )\cdot 2 = \begin{pmatrix} -35 \\ 19 \end{pmatrix} $$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We add the projection $\begin{pmatrix} -35 \\ 19 \end{pmatrix} $ to $\mathbf{v}$ to get the vector
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\mathbf{v} + \mathbf{w} = \begin{pmatrix} -7 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} $$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The unit vector perpendicular to $\mathbf{v} + \mathbf{w}$ is
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$\mathbf{u} = \frac{\mathbf{v} + \mathbf{w}}{|\mathbf{v} + \mathbf{w}|} = \frac{\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}}{\sqrt {(-2)^2 + 3^2}}= \frac{ \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}}{5} = \frac{2}{5} \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 1.5 \end{pmatrix} $$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The area of the parallelogram formed by $\mathbf{0}$, $\mathbf{v}$, $\mathbf{w}$, and $\mathbf{v} + \mathbf{w}$ is $|\mathbf{u}| |\mathbf{w}| = 0.{008}{114} \boxed{\mathrm{x}} .$ Crimea. Crimea ideal ; Morse
