[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 2: Convert $10101_3$ to base 10.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The given number is $10101_3$. We can break it down as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m First, break down the number into its digit values:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - $1$ in base 3
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - $0$ in base 3
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - $1$ in base 3
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - $0$ in base 3
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - $1$ in base 3
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 3: Continue the breakdown as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - $1 \times 3^4 = 1 \times 81 = 81$ (This is $3^3$)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - $0 \times 3^3 = 0$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - $1 \times 3^2 = 1 \times 9 = 9$ (This is $3^2$)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - $0 \times 3^2 = 0$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - $1 \times 3 = 1$ (This is $3^1$)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Step 4: Add up the values:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $81 + 9 + 1 = 81 + 10 = 91$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
