[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Find the projection of $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$ onto the plane $3x - y + 4z = 0.$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the projection of the vector $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$ onto the plane $3x - y + 4z = 0$, we first need to find the normal vector to the plane. The normal vector is parallel to the vector $\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Then, we can find the projection of the vector $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$ onto this normal vector.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The projection of a vector $\begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \\ c \end{pmatrix}$ onto a normal vector $\begin{pmatrix} p \\ q \\ r \end{pmatrix}$ is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \text{proj}_{\begin{pmatrix} p \\ q \\ r \end{pmatrix}} \begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \\ c \end{pmatrix} = \frac{a}{p^2 + q^2 + r^2} \begin{pmatrix} p \\ q \\ r \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let's find the projection of $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$ onto $\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}$, then scale this projection by a factor of 3 (to match the length of the vector $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$ to the length of the normal vector $\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}$).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \text{projection} = \frac{1}{3^2 + 2^2 + 3^2} \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \frac{1}{3^2 + 2^2 + 3^2}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \text{projection} = \frac{1}{3^2 + 2^2 + 3^2} \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \frac{1}{9 + 4 + 9}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \text{projection} = \frac{1}{3^2 + 2^2 + 3^2} \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \frac{1}{22}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \text{projection} = \frac{1}{70} \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \frac{1}{22}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \text{projection} = \frac{1}{70} \cdot \frac{3}{22} \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} = \frac{3}{1540} \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \text{projection} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{9}{1540} \\ -\frac{3}{1540} \\ \frac{12}{1540} \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Simplifying the fractions:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \text{projection} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{9}{1540} \\ -\frac{3}{1540} \\ \frac{3}{770} \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Thus, the projection of $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$ onto the plane $3x - y + 4z = 0$ is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} \frac{9}{1540} \\ -\frac{3}{1540} \\ \frac{3}{770} \end{pmatrix}}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
