[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The amount of money a certain company has can be modeled with the line $y=-265x+2800$, where $x$ is the number of workers the company decides to hire. What is the maximum number of workers the company can hire before the company has no money left and goes bankrupt?
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m At the point where $y=0$, we find that $0=-265x+2800 $, which leads to $265x=2800$ and finally $x=10.1896...\$, which cannot be an integer. So we can calculate the number of workers after hiring 10 workers as a test variable. $N$:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{cases}-265 \cdot N + 2800 = 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 265 \cdot (N+1) = 265 \cdot 10 = 2650 \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m From the above equation, we find that $N=39$, which means the maximum order amount of workers is 39 workers.
