[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m First, we square both sides of the equation to remove square roots.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \(\left(\sqrt{1 + \sqrt{2y-3}}\right)^2 = \left(\sqrt{6}\right)^2\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \(\Rightarrow 1 + \sqrt{2y-3} = 6\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Next, we isolate the square root term on one side of the equation.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \(\Rightarrow \sqrt{2y-3} = 6 - 1\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \(\Rightarrow \sqrt{2y-3} = 5\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Finally, we take the square of both sides to solve for \(y\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \(\Rightarrow 2y-3 = 25\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \(\Rightarrow 2y = 28\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \(\Rightarrow y = 14\)
