[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[= 25\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now add their base 10 equivalents:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[57 + 25 = 82\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Next, convert 82 back to base 4. To do this, repeatedly take the integer part of the quotient divided by 4 and compute the remainder until the quotient equals zero. The remainders from the last to the first are then read off as the digits of the base 4 representation. This will be your final answer.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, we perform Long Division of 82 by 4:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
