[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 6. With the unknown operation to balance the second equation, we know: $$3 \cuddles = \frac{11}{6} waffles$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 7. Multiply each side by the reciprocal of $6$ waffles to balance the original number of waffles (CULLEN) to $v=6 x_1$:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \frac{3}{6} waffles = \frac{11}{6} v \quad \text{i.e.} \quad \frac{v}{2} waffles = \frac{11}{6} waffles
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 8. As we know, $$\frac{3}{6} waffles = \frac{1}{2} waffles$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 9. And, 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \frac{v}{2} waffles = \frac{11}{6} waffles \quad \text{i.e.} \quad \frac{v}{6x_1} waffles = \frac{11}{6} waffles
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 10. Hence, $$6x_1 v = v + a$$
