[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. **Identify the general form of the function:**
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    The given function is in the form of \( y = a \sin(bx + c) + d \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. **Understand the amplitude of the function:**
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - The amplitude \( |a| \) determines the height of the sine wave.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - The spreading factor \( |b| \) determines the phase shift.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. **Interpret the given graph:**
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - The graph shows that \( y = a \sin(bx + c) + d \) oscillates between \( -2 \) and \( 2 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4. **Analyze the oscillation:**
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - The sine function \( \sin(bx + c) \) oscillates between \(-1\) and \(1\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - Therefore, the amplitude \( |a| \) of \( y = a \sin(bx + c) \) is 2.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 5. **Determine the period of the function:**
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - The period of the function \( y = a \sin(bx + c) + d \) is \( \frac{2\pi}{b} \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - From the given graph, we see that the period is \( \frac{2\pi}{b} \), which can be expressed as \( \frac{2\pi}{2} = \pi \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 6. **Set up the equation for the period:**
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    - The period \( \pi \) corresponds to \( b = 2 \) because the period of \( \sin(bx + c) \) is inversely proportional to \( b \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
