[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    13 & b & c \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    a' & 23 & c' \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    a' & b' & 42 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Given that $a \ne 13$ and $x \ne 0$, we can derive:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    a' + b' + c' = 0
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. Now, let's look at the expression we need to evaluate:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \frac{a'}{a' - 13} + \frac{b'}{b' - 23} + \frac{c'}{c' - 42}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4. Substituting the relationships from steps above:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    13 & b & c \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    a - (a - 13) & 23 & c -(23) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    a - (a - 13) & b - (23) & 42 -(42)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    Thus:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    13 & b & c \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    a + 13 & 23 & c - 23 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    a + 13 & b - 23 & 0
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 5. Notice that the determinants of the resulting matrix $D_3 \times D_4$ (where $D_3$ and $D_4$ do not change the value for $x$):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    D_3 \times D_4 = \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    23 & c - 23 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    23 & 0
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 6. Back-substituting the relationship $a + 13 = 0$:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    a = -13
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    Substituting back into the matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    D_3 \times D_4 = \begin{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    23 & c - 23 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    23 & 0
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 7. Since $c - 23 \ne 0$, the relative differences between the columns won't contribute significantly to the overall matrix.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 8. We need to evaluate the final expression:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \frac{a}{a - 13} + \frac{b}{b - 23} + \frac{c}{c - 42}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 9. As $-13$ is smaller than 13, $a \ne 15$. Given the relationship $a + b + c = 13$, we maximize $a - 13$ (making $a$ as large as possible while still satisfying the condition for the other columns):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    a = -13, b = 0, c = 45
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 10. Finally, substituting these values:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m     \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m     \frac{-13}{-13 - 13} + \frac{0}{0 - 23} + \frac{45}{45 - 42}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m     \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    Result:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m     \(\boxed{x = 15}\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Thus, achieving the maximum sum is achieved at the roots (-13, 0, 45) or (15), making two areas.
