[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the distance between two points \((x_1, y_1)\) and \((x_2, y_2)\) in a Cartesian plane, we use the distance formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m d = \sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Given the points \((-2, 4)\) and \((3, -8)\), we can identify:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m (x_1, y_1) = (-2, 4)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m (x_2, y_2) = (3, -8)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, substitute these values into the distance formula:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m d = \sqrt{(3 - (-2))^2 + (-8 - 4)^2}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Simplify inside the parentheses:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m d = \sqrt{(3 + 2)^2 + (-8 - 4)^2}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m d = \sqrt{5^2 + (-12)^2}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Calculate the squares:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m d = \sqrt{25 + 144}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Add the results:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m d = \sqrt{169}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Take the square root of 169:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m d = 13
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
