[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Open number foundations are a crosscutting disciplinary theme throughout mathematics class, and bifurcation theory and differential equations are two, perhaps surprisingly, relevant and fascinating modern subfields of mathematics in general. Solving bifurcation equations, for instance, is the ultimate project of the unique flow associated with homoclinic bifurcation -- a bifurcation that -- in its very nature -- produces chaotic dynamics. That's what makes bifurcation theory interesting, and for which it received a Nobel Prize.
