[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m A solid box is 15 cm by 10 cm by 8 cm. A new solid is formed by removing a cube 3 cm on a side from each corner of this box. What percent of the original volume is removed?
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To calculate the percent of the original volume removed, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. **Calculate the original volume of the solid:**
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The original box has dimensions \(15 \, \text{cm} \times 10 \, \text{cm} \times 8 \, \text{cm}\). The volume \(V_{\text{original}}\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m V_{\text{original}} = 15 \times 10 \times 8 = 1200 \, \text{cm}^3
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. **Calculate the volume of the cube removed:**
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Each cube has a side length of 3 cm. The volume \(V_{\text{cube}}\) of one cube is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m V_{\text{cube}} = 3 \times 3 \times 3 = 27 \, \text{cm}^3
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m There are 4 such cubes removed from each corner of the box. The total volume \(V_{\text{removed}}\) removed is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m V_{\text{removed}} = 4 \times 27 = 108 \, \text{cm}^3
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. **Calculate the percent of the original volume removed:**
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The percentage \(P\) of the original volume that is removed is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m P = \left( \frac{V_{\text{removed}}}{V_{\text{original}}} \right) \times 100
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Substituting the values we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m P = \left( \frac{108}{1200} \right) \times 100
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Simplify the fraction:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m P = \left( \frac{108}{1200} \right) = \frac{108 \div 36}{1200 \div 36} = \frac{3}{33} \approx 0.0909
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Finally, convert to a percentage:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m P \approx 9.09\%
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Thus, the percent of the original volume that is removed is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \boxed{9.09\%}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
