[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Complementary angles are those that add up to 90 degrees. Conversely, the sum of two complementary angles is equal to 90 degrees. So let’s denote the measure of the angle as x. Consequently, its complement also measures x, inclusive of the fact that one angle is double the other by double value.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Given that the sum of the two angles cannot exceed 90 degrees in any practical application and also that they are complementary, after mathematical manipulation, it is apparent that \( x + x = 90 \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Hence, \( 2 \cdot x = 90 ° \), meaning,
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ \boxed{x} = 45° \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Winter's asleep.<|endoftext|>
