[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We can approach this problem by selecting points on each of the sides of the ramp and then using the dot product formula. The dot product is calculated as the product of the corresponding coordinates of two vectors. We will choose three distinct points on each of the sides of the ramp such that the dot product of these points is 20.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let's say the points are P1, P2, and P3 (on the sides of length 12 m, 8 m, 7 m respectively). We can choose P1, P2, and P3 such that the dot product of P1 and Sp is 20, P2 and Sp is 20, and P3 and Sp is 20. This means we have three distinct points, P1, P2, and P3, where |dot(P1, Sp)| = 20.
