[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To solve the equation \(\log_4 x + \log_2 x^2 = 10\), we will first simplify the left-hand side of the equation. We start by combining the logarithms using the properties of logarithms.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The property \(\log_b a + \log_b c = \log_b (ac)\) allows us to combine the terms on the left-hand side:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \log_4 x + \log_2 x^2 = \log_4 x + \log_2 (x^2) = \log_4 x + \log_2 (x^2).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Next, we use the exponent property \(\log_b b^k = k\) to simplify the second term on the right-hand side:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \log_2 (x^2) = 2 \log_2 x.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So the equation becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \log_4 x + 2 \log_2 x = 10.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We can rewrite \(2 \log_2 x\) as \(\log_4 x^2\), because \(\log_b (a^c) = c \log_b a\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \log_4 x + \log_4 x^2 = 10.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Next, we use the property of logarithms \(\log_a (a^b) = b\) to combine the two logarithms:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \log_4 (x \cdot x^2) = 10.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \log_4 (x^3) = 10.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Since \(10 = 4^{\log_4 10}\) by the change of base formula for logarithms, we can rewrite the equation as:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \log_4 (x^3) = \log_4 (4^{\log_4 10}).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The right-hand side simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4^{\log_4 10} = 10.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m This is true because \(4 = 2^2\) and \(2 = 4^{\frac{1}{2}}\), so \(\log_4 (2^2) = \log_4 (4^{\frac{1}{2}})\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Thus, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \log_4 (x^3) = 10.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We can rewrite the left-hand side as (\(4^1\)) and \((3^1)\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3^1 = 10.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Taking the logarithm base 4 of both sides gives:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \log_4 3 = 1.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To solve for \(x\), we exponentiate both sides of the equation \(\log_4 3 = 1\) with base 4:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4^1 = 3.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So the solution is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m x^3 = 3.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Taking the cube root of both sides gives:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m x = \sqrt[3]{3}.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, the solution to the equation is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \boxed{\sqrt[3]{3}}.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
