[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To determine the greatest possible length of the cut lumber, we need to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of the lengths of the three pieces of timber: 48, 72, and 40 feet. This is because the GCD will give us the length of the lumber that is the greatest possible unit length to form the largest possible sets of equal units (logs). The divisors of these numbers will be our lower lengths when forming logs of equal length.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m First, we'll find the GCD of 48 and 72. Then, we'll find the GCD of that with either 40 or any other of the original lengths. The number that occurs in both places is our answer.
