[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m First of all, the license plate has two letters and two digits, so we have 3 choices for each character.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Then, we need to consider the odd and even digits. There are 5 odd digits (1, 3, 5, 7, 9), so we have \frac{5}{2} = 2.5 combinations to choose the odd digit. Since we can't have half digits, we round up to 3 odd digits.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Similarly, there are 5 even digits (0, 2, 4, 6, 8), so we have \frac{5}{2} = 2.5 combinations to choose the even digit.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, there are \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3 \text{ odd digits} \times 2.5 = 7.5\text{ combinations}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m and \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3 \text{ even digits} \times 2.5 = 7.5\text{ combinations}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Adding these, we get a total of 15 combinations.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
