[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m How many cubic feet are in three cubic yards?
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Certainly, here's how you can find out how many cubic feet are in three cubic yards:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. First, let's determine the total number of cubic feet in a cubic yard. Since a cubic yard is 12 inches (3 feet) by 12 inches (3 feet), its surface area is as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    12 \times 12 = 144 \text{ square inches}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Next, we need to convert this area into cubic feet. There are 3 feet in a yard, so a yard is 3 feet by 3 feet (or 9 feet in total):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    9 \text{ feet} \times 9 \text{ feet} \times 3 \text{ feet} = 243 \text{ square feet}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. We divide our total cubic yard area by the area of one cubic foot to find out how many cubic feet are in a yard:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \frac{243 \text{ square feet}}{144 \text{ square inches per square foot}} = \frac{243/144}{1} \text{ cubic feet} = \frac{1}{6} \text{ cubic feet}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4. Since we have yards, multiply this result by 3 to get the number of cubic feet in three cubic yards:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \frac{1}{6} \times 3 = \frac{3}{6} = 0.5 \text{ cubic feet}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Hence,
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \boxed{0.5}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
