[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  To find a three-digit number with a units digit of 2 and a hundreds digit of 4 that is divisible by 9, we can use the rule of divisibility by 9. A number is divisible by 9 if the sum of its digits is divisible by 9.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The sum of the digits in the desired number will be 2 + 4 + 0 (since the units digit is 2 and the hundreds digit is 4) = 6. So we need to find a number with a digit sum of 6 that is divisible by 9.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The LCM (Least Common Multiple) of 6 and 9 is 18, so the desired number must be divisible by 18.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The possible three-digit numbers with units digit 2 and hundreds digit 4 that are divisible by 18 are 342, 562, 782, 902, and 902.
