[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m What must be the value of the coefficient $c$ in $P(x)=x^3+2x^2+cx+10$, in order for $x-5$ to be a factor of $P$?
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The polynomial \(P(x) = x^3 + 2x^2 + cx + 10\) appears to be \(P(x) = (x - 5)Q(x)\), where \(Q(x)\) is a cubic polynomial. When the remainder is zero, we have \(P(x) = (x - 5) \cdot R_1(x)\), where \(R_1(x)\) is a quadratic polynomial. Since \(P(x)\) itself is a cubic polynomial, \(R_1(x)\) must also be a cubic polynomial. Therefore, we can write \(P(x)\) as:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[P(x) = (x - 5)(x^2 + px + q)\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the values of \(c\) and \(p\), we need to expand the product on the right-hand side. Expanding the right-hand side, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m (x - 5)(x^2 + px + q) = x^3 + (p - 5)x^2 + (q - 5p)x - 5q
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m By comparing coefficients with \(P(x) = x^3 + 2x^2 + cx + 10\), we get the following system of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. \(p - 5 = 2\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. \(q - 5p = c\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. \(-5q = 10\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m From equation 1, we solve for \(p\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ p - 5 = 2 \implies p = 7 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Substitute \(p = 7\) into equation 3:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ -5q = 10 \implies q = -2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, substitute \(p = 7\) into equation 2 to find \(c\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ c = q - 5p = -2 - 5 \cdot 7 = -2 - 35 = -37 \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, the value of the coefficient \(c\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \boxed{-37}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
