[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ $d$ be nonnegative real numbers such that $a + b + c + d = 1.$  Find the maximum value of
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + d^2.\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We start by noting the sum constraint.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m a + b + c + d &= 1\\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*} 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, we apply the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality on the matrix pair 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m ($ab + ac + ad + ac$ and $b c + bc + bd + bc$).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m (ab + ac + ad + ac) &\ge \sqrt{(ab)(ac + bc + bd + bc)} \tag{C-S}.\ \ \ \ \ \ \
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m By multiplying $C-S$ by $\frac{a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + d^2}{1}$,
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \frac{1}{1} \cdot \left((ab + ac + ad + ac)\right)^2 &\ge \left(\frac{a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + d^2}{1}\right) \cdot \sqrt{(ab)(ac + bc + bd + bc)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1^2 &\le \frac{(ab + ac + ad + ac)^2}{2}\cdot (ac + bd + bd) \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1 &\le \frac{(ab + ac + ad + ac)^2(a + b) - 6]{2} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1 &\le \frac{(ab + ac + ad + ac)^2(a + b)}{2a + b + c + d} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1 &\le \frac{(ab + ac + ad + ac)^2}{a + b +c + d} \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1 &\le \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1 &\le \frac{1}{4}.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Hence, $a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + d^2 \le 3.$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m It is clear that equality above is attained for $a=c=f=d=1/7,$ which gives us $(a,b,c,d) = (\frac{1}{7}, \frac{1}{7}, \frac{1}{7}, \frac{1}{7}).$ The maximum value of $a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + d^2$ 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m is 3.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
