[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the surface area of a cube, we need to consider the area of each set of cells that make up one of the faces of the cube. In this case, we have four faces, each of which is a square with a side length of 3 inches. 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The surface area of each square face is equal to the side length squared (since the area of a square is calculated by multiplying the length of one side by itself), so each face has an area of \(3 \times 3 = 9\) square inches. 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Since there are four faces, the total surface area of the cube is \(4 \times 9 = 36\) square inches. 
