[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To solve this problem, we need to predict the difference between 1335 and 40, because we want to know how many books are left over and not if there are more or less, because the question asks how many books are left over. So, the difference will be 40x1335, which is equivalent to 4, which simplifies to 1 ≠ 0.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $\therefore$ The total number of books left over is $[15-1]=1335-1335=0$. So, Melvin has 0 books left over.
