[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \log z - \log x = -7
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We want to find the value of \(a\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. Combine the three equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \log x - \log y = a
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \log y - \log z = 15
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \log z - \log x = -7
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. Rewrite the second and third equations using properties of logarithms:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \log y - \log y = \log y - \log z \implies a = 15
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \log z - \log z = -7 \implies a = -7
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So far, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m a = 15
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m a = -7
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 3. Check for consistency by substituting \(a\) back into the original equations.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 4. Check \(\log x - \log y = 15\) with \(a = 15\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \log x - \log y = 15
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Using properties of logarithms on both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \log \left( \frac{x}{y} \right) = \log 15
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 5. Since \(\log y = \log 15\), it follows that:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \log x = 15
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Hence:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m x = 15^{15}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 6. Check \(\log y - \log z = -7\) with \(a = 15\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \log y - \log z = -7
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Using properties of logarithms on both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \log \left( \frac{y}{z} \right) = -7
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 7. Since \(\log 1 = 0\), it follows that:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \frac{y}{z} = 10^{-7}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m y = -7 \times 10^{10}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 8. Finally \(\log z - \log x = -7\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \log z - \log y = -7
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Convert \(\log z\) from base 10:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
