[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the distance between the points \((-5, -2)\) and \((7, 3)\), we can use the distance formula. The distance formula between two points \((x_1, y_1)\) and \((x_2, y_2)\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m d = \sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Here, \((x_1, y_1) = (-5, -2)\) and \((x_2, y_2) = (7, 3)\). Plugging these values into the formula, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m d = \sqrt{(7 - (-5))^2 + (3 - (-2))^2}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m First, simplify inside the parentheses:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m d = \sqrt{(7 + 5)^2 + (3 + 2)^2} = \sqrt{(12)^2 + (5)^2}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Next, calculate the squares:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m d = \sqrt{144 + 25}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Add the results:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m d = \sqrt{169}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Finally, take the square root:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m d = 13
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, the distance between the points \((-5, -2)\) and \((7, 3)\) is \(\boxed{13}\).<|endoftext|>
