[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To solve for the product \(xy\), we need to first determine the values of \(x\) and \(y\) from the given equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 1. \(2x - 9y = 14\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 2. \(6x = 42 + y\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We will use the second equation to express \(y\) in terms of \(x\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[6x = 42 + y\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[y = 6x - 42\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Next, substitute \(y = 6x - 42\) into the first equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[2x - 9(6x - 42) = 14\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Simplify the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[2x - 54x + 378 = 14\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[-52x + 378 = 14\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[-52x = 14 - 378\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[-52x = -364\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[x = \frac{-364}{-52}\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[x = 7\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now that we have \(x = 7\), we can find \(y\) using the expression \(y = 6x - 42\):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[y = 6(7) - 42\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[y = 42 - 42\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[y = 0\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now we have \(x = 7\) and \(y = 0\). The value of the product \(xy\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[xy = 7 \times 0 = 0\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, the value of the product \(xy\) is \(\boxed{0}\).<|endoftext|>
