[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The areas of three of the faces of a right, rectangular prism are $24 \hspace{.6mm} \mathrm{cm}^2$, $32 \hspace{.6mm} \mathrm{cm}^2$, and $48 \hspace{.6mm} \mathrm{cm}^2$. What is the volume of the prism, in cubic centimeters?
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The volume of a right rectangular prism can be found by multiplying the length, width, and height together. In this case, we are given the areas of three of the faces, so we can write the following equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \text{Area of base} &= l \cdot w \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 24 &= l \cdot w \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \text{Area of bottom} &= l \cdot h \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 32 &= l \cdot h \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \text{Area of top} &= w \cdot h \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 48 &= w \cdot h \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We can rearrange each equation to express the height \( h \) in terms of the length \( l \) and other variables:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m l \cdot w &= 24 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m l \cdot h &= 32 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m w \cdot h &= 48 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We can then use these expressions to find the values of \( l \), \( w \), and \( h \). Let's start with the first set of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m l \cdot w &= 24 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We can express \( w \) in terms of \( l \):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m w = \frac{24}{l}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Next, we substitute \( w \) into the second equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \left(\frac{24}{l}\right) \cdot h &= 32 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We can express \( h \) in terms of \( l \):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m h = \frac{32}{\frac{24}{l}} = \frac{32l}{24} = \frac{4l}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Finally, we substitute \( w \) and \( h \) into the third equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \frac{24}{l} \cdot \frac{4l}{3} &= 48 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Simplify the left side:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \frac{24 \cdot 4l}{3l} &= 48 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \frac{96}{3l} &= 48 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \frac{32}{l} &= 48
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We can solve for \( l \):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m l = \frac{32}{48} = \frac{2}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now we substitute \( l = \frac{2}{3} \) back into the expressions for \( w \) and \( h \):
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m w &= \frac{24}{\frac{2}{3}} = 24 \cdot \frac{3}{2} = 36 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m h &= \frac{4 \cdot \frac{2}{3}}{3} = \frac{8}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now we can find the volume of the prism by multiplying the three dimensions:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \text{Volume} &= l \cdot w \cdot h \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= \left(\frac{2}{3} \cdot 36 \cdot \frac{4}{3}\right) \cdot \left(\frac{3}{2} \cdot \frac{8}{3}\right) \cdot 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= \left(18 \cdot 4\right) \cdot 4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= 72 \cdot 4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m &= \boxed{288}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
