[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let's solve this step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m The sum of the powers of $11$ from $11^1$ to $11^9$ can be grouped into sets of three terms each.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$(11 + 10) + (11^2 + 11) + (11^3 + 11^2 + 11)$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$= 21 + 345 + 3411$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, we add the +1s at the end:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$21+345+3411+1$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m And finally, we sum up the first 3+1=4 terms of $11^k$:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$11^1 + 11^2 + 11^3 + \ldots + 11^3 = 11(1 + 11 + 11^2) = 11(334) = 3674$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, the complete sum is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$3674 + 1 = 3675$$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m And the tens digit of this sum is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$7$$
