[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let's start by analyzing the geometric relationships in the triangle.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \(AB = AC = 25\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m - \(BC = 23\)
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Points \(D, E,\) and \(F\) are on sides \(\overline{AB}, \overline{BC},\) and \(\overline{AC}\) respectively, such that \(\overline{DE}\) is parallel to \(\overline{AC}\) and \(\overline{EF}\) is parallel to \(\overline{AB}\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m First, note that since \(\overline{DE}\) is parallel to \(\overline{AC}\), and \(\overline{EF}\) is parallel to \(\overline{AB}\), triangles \( \triangle ADE \) and \( \triangle ABC \) are similar, and triangles \( \triangle BDE \) and \( \triangle ABC \) are also similar.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Since \( \triangle ADE \propto \triangle ABC \) and \( \overline{DE} \parallel \overline{AC} \), \( \angle D = \angle A \), which implies \(\triangle ADE \sim \triangle ABC\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Similarly, since \(\triangle BDE \propto \triangle ABC \) and \( \overline{EF} \parallel \overline{AB} \), \( \angle E = \angle A \), which implies \(\triangle BDE \sim \triangle ABC\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Given that \(DE \parallel AB\), \(EF \parallel AC\), and considering the similarity of triangles, the segments \(AD\) and \(AF\) are proportional to the corresponding segments, and since \(DE \parallel AC\), the segments \(EF\) and \(BC\) also have the same length as the corresponding segments in \( \triangle ABC \).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, \(\triangle AEF\) is similar to \(\triangle ABC\) and \(\angle AEF = \angle ABC\) because \(\overline{DE} \parallel \overline{AC}\), \(\overline{EF} \parallel \overline{AB}\), and \(\angle DEF = \angle ACB\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, using similarity of triangles, \(\overline{AE} = EC = \frac{AB}{2} = 10\) and \(\overline{DF} = FA = \frac{AC}{2} = 5\).
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, the perimeter of parallelogram \(ADEF\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[ \text{Perimeter} = 2(AD + AE) + 2(DF + EF) = 2(10 + 10) + 2(5 + 5) = 340. \]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Therefore, the perimeter of parallelogram \(ADEF\) is \(\boxed{340}\).<|endoftext|>
