[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Find the minimum value of $\sin^4 x + \cos^4 x.$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the minimum value of $\sin^4 x + \cos^4 x$, use the trigonometric identity 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \[\sin^4 x + \cos^4 x = (\sin^2 x + \cos^2 x)^2 - 2\sin^2 x \cos^2 x = 1 - 2\sin^2 x \cos^2 x\]
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Considering the range of  $\sin^2 x$ and $\cos^2 x$, the function becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $ \begin{cases} -1 \leq \sin^2 x \leq 1 \\ -1\leq \cos^2 x\leq 1 \end{cases}$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Start with the upper-lower range, i.e $(0,1)$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Simplify:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $ \begin{cases} -1 \leq \sin^2 x \leq 1 \\ -1 \leq \cos^2 x \leq 1 \end{cases}$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $ \begin{cases} -1 \leq \sin^4 x \leq 1 \\ -1 \leq \cos^4 x \leq 1 \end{cases}$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $ \begin{cases} -1 \leq \sin^4 x \leq 1 \\ -1 \leq \cos^4 x \leq 1 \end{cases}$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $ -1 \leq \sin^4 x \leq 1 \cap -1 \leq \cos^4 x \leq 1$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $ -1 \leq \sin^4 x \leq 1 \Rightarrow - 1 \leq (\sin^2 x)^2$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $ -1 \leq \cos^4 x \leq 1 \Rightarrow 0 \leq (\cos^2 x)^2$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m  
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m From the $$ \begin{cases} -1 \leq \sin^4 x \leq 1 \\ -1 \leq \cos^4 x \leq 1 \end{cases}$$, we find the lower boundary for both, e.g when $\sin^4 x=0$, $\cos^4 x=0$, at $x=0,45^{\circ}$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Substitute back the case:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $\sin^4 x+\cos^4 x=-1+0=   -1$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m In fact, the answer is $ -1$<|endoftext|>
