[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Let $\#$ be the relation defined by $A \# B = A^2 + B^2$. If $A \# 5 = 169$, what is the positive value of $A$?
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find the positive value of $A$ given the equation $\#$, we can solve for $A$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We start by substituting $5$ and the given solution ($A$) into the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \text{A} \# 5 &= 169 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m A^2 + \text{5}^2 &= 169 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m A^2 + 25 &= 169 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m A^2 &= 169 - 25 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m A^2 &= 144 \\
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m A &= \boxed{12} \quad
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m \end{align*}
