[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m I'll start by understanding the problem. Lines $l$ and $k$ are parallel, and $m\angle A = 120^\circ$ and $m\angle C = 80^\circ$. I need to find $m\angle B$.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To start by finding $m\angle C$, I will use the direct angle subtraction method:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $$m\angle B = m\angle A + m\angle C$$
