[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m A recipe calls for $\frac14$ teaspoon of salt for each quart of water. How many quarts of water will be used for two teaspoons of salt?
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Sure, I can help you with that.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m We know that $\frac14$ teaspoon of salt will be used for each quart of water.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m To find out how many quarts of water will be used for two teaspoons of salt, we can set up a simple proportion.
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $\frac{\frac14$\ teaspoon of salt}{1 quart of water} = $\frac{2$\ teaspoons of salt}{2 quarts of water}$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m Now, cross-multiply and solve for the unknown number of quarts of water:
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $\frac14$\ teaspoon of salt * $2^th$ quarts of water = 1$\times$2$\times$（ teaspoons of salt divided by 2 quarts of water）$\frac{1}{2}$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $\frac 14 \times 2 = 2$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m $\boxed{1}$
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=1078428)[0m So, 1 quadruple of water ($2$ quarts) will be used for two teaspoons of salt.<|endoftext|>
